WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:17.955
I think women
can do anything.

2
00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:20.591
Well, I mean,
just because they can,

3
00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:22.392
doesn't mean they should,
right?

4
00:00:24.193 --> 00:00:27.397
Think about women
fixing cars,

5
00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:29.399
driving a taxi,

6
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:31.602
installing
some drywall.

7
00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:33.737
- Why not?
- No.

8
00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:35.171
Look, trust me.

9
00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:37.908
A girl like you,
you don't really want this.

10
00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:40.978
- A girl like me?
- Mm-hm.

11
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.112
I mean, I want
all my options available

12
00:00:43.246 --> 00:00:44.582
so I can decide
for myself.

13
00:00:44.715 --> 00:00:47.383
Ah, Miss Independent.

14
00:00:47.518 --> 00:00:50.253
That's right.

15
00:00:50.386 --> 00:00:52.656
- That's me.
- I love it.

16
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.224
Mm...

17
00:00:55.358 --> 00:00:57.460
- Come here.
- Hm...

18
00:01:01.832 --> 00:01:04.367
Oh, mm...

19
00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.704
Except
you're sitting here,

20
00:01:06.837 --> 00:01:10.340
eating my food,
enjoying my view.

21
00:01:10.473 --> 00:01:11.842
By choice.

22
00:01:11.976 --> 00:01:13.911
Mm, I chose you
to join me.

23
00:01:15.646 --> 00:01:18.649
- I chose to make you notice me.
- Ah, mm-mm.

24
00:01:18.782 --> 00:01:21.018
- That is not your choice, Sabina.
- Mm.

25
00:01:21.184 --> 00:01:22.653
That is God's gift to you.

26
00:01:25.388 --> 00:01:27.490
Gosh...

27
00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.125
But don't you think
it's sort of

28
00:01:29.258 --> 00:01:32.896
what you do with those gifts
that really matters?

29
00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.263
Mmm.

30
00:01:34.397 --> 00:01:35.465
- Every one of us.
- Mm?

31
00:01:35.599 --> 00:01:37.901
Men, women.

32
00:01:38.035 --> 00:01:40.004
We all just wanna
fulfill our potential,

33
00:01:40.136 --> 00:01:41.872
live our heart's desires.

34
00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:44.173
That's the kind of world
I wanna live in.

35
00:01:44.307 --> 00:01:46.175
Ah.

36
00:01:46.309 --> 00:01:49.780
Well, my world
is me making millions

37
00:01:49.913 --> 00:01:51.849
with you by my side.

38
00:01:53.584 --> 00:01:54.785
Hm?

39
00:01:54.918 --> 00:01:56.520
It's just that I'm so good

40
00:01:56.654 --> 00:01:58.656
at so many things.

41
00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:00.490
- Oh, yeah?
- Yeah.

42
00:02:00.624 --> 00:02:02.291
Like what?

43
00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:03.961
- Well...
- Hm?

44
00:02:04.094 --> 00:02:06.030
At my job,

45
00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:08.832
it's actually considered
a huge advantage to be a woman.

46
00:02:08.966 --> 00:02:11.135
Hm.

47
00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.736
Yeah,
if you're beautiful,

48
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.139
nothing else
is really expected of you.

49
00:02:15.271 --> 00:02:16.540
And if you're not,

50
00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:18.876
you're pretty much
rendered invisible.

51
00:02:20.343 --> 00:02:22.846
- And in my line of work,
- Mm...

52
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.183
invisibility,
low expectations...

53
00:02:27.316 --> 00:02:29.520
they come in very handy.

54
00:02:30.521 --> 00:02:32.221
Housewife, sounds like.

55
00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.391
Nothing wrong with being a housewife.

56
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:39.055
Just not my choice.

57
00:02:39.163 --> 00:02:42.166
- I don't speak Portuguese.
- I know.

58
00:02:48.371 --> 00:02:49.606
Yeah, that's it.

59
00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:10.661
- Did you know...
- What?

60
00:03:10.794 --> 00:03:12.896
That it takes men
an additional seven seconds

61
00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.599
to perceive a woman
as a threat compared to a man.

62
00:03:17.201 --> 00:03:18.569
Isn't that wild?

63
00:03:22.773 --> 00:03:24.208
- Who are you?
- Who, me?

64
00:03:27.376 --> 00:03:28.912
I'm just the decoy, stud.

65
00:03:37.521 --> 00:03:39.189
- How many?
- Nine!

66
00:03:39.322 --> 00:03:40.524
Send the lot.

67
00:03:47.865 --> 00:03:51.568
You stole aid money from women
and children and refugees!

68
00:03:51.702 --> 00:03:52.903
It's called embezzlement!

69
00:03:54.972 --> 00:03:57.141
"Embezzlement"?
That's fancy.

70
00:04:04.848 --> 00:04:07.985
- You must be the accountant.
- Who are you?

71
00:04:09.352 --> 00:04:10.486
Open the safe.

72
00:04:10.621 --> 00:04:13.757
Oh, baby, baby,
you swiped right!

73
00:04:13.891 --> 00:04:15.592
I'm your girlfriend now!

74
00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.696
Everything on the bottom row.
Let's go.

75
00:04:21.665 --> 00:04:25.169
You're not cut out for this.
I recommend a new line of work.

76
00:04:29.606 --> 00:04:30.874
Bosley!

77
00:04:31.008 --> 00:04:33.177
Evening, Angels.

78
00:04:33.309 --> 00:04:36.580
Well, all this looks
very promising.

79
00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:38.115
Outstanding.

80
00:04:38.248 --> 00:04:40.951
But what about
Australian Jonny?

81
00:04:41.084 --> 00:04:42.418
Ta-da!

82
00:04:42.553 --> 00:04:44.154
- Oh, you're gonna regret this.
- Yeah.

83
00:04:44.288 --> 00:04:45.756
I was gonna
give you the world.

84
00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:47.958
The thing is, is you just talk
way too much.

85
00:04:48.091 --> 00:04:50.294
You're super clingy
and come on way too strong.

86
00:04:50.426 --> 00:04:51.895
You are the most
incredible woman

87
00:04:52.029 --> 00:04:53.831
- I've ever met.
- I know.

88
00:04:53.964 --> 00:04:56.567
So that's four months'
surveillance, two countries

89
00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.970
and the most embarrassing date
I have ever been on in my life.

90
00:05:00.103 --> 00:05:01.872
- Are we good?
- I will address this

91
00:05:02.005 --> 00:05:04.141
to the
U.S. Justice Department,

92
00:05:04.274 --> 00:05:07.476
along with, uh,
all your new friends here.

93
00:05:07.611 --> 00:05:09.847
- We're good to go.
- Sweet.

94
00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.182
I'm out of here, man.
I'm gonna take a week off,

95
00:05:12.316 --> 00:05:13.884
party my ass off
on a Thai beach.

96
00:05:14.017 --> 00:05:15.519
Jane,
you should give it a shot:

97
00:05:15.652 --> 00:05:17.988
beaches, letting someone
play with your, uh...

98
00:05:19.455 --> 00:05:21.525
I have fun
in my own ways.

99
00:05:21.658 --> 00:05:23.392
Oh. Cool.

100
00:05:23.527 --> 00:05:26.495
You sharpen
your samurai swords at night?

101
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.065
Cosplay Catwoman?

102
00:05:28.198 --> 00:05:29.867
I'd actually pay
to see that.

103
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.002
Occasionally eat gluten
at night and feel...

104
00:05:33.503 --> 00:05:34.838
That was fun.

105
00:05:34.972 --> 00:05:36.506
So who were they?

106
00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.043
You were in the presence
of Angels.

107
00:05:41.178 --> 00:05:43.213
But the question is, Jonny...

108
00:05:45.182 --> 00:05:47.251
who are you?

109
00:06:43.707 --> 00:06:45.474
Hey, Ingrid.

110
00:06:45.609 --> 00:06:47.544
You are late.
Mr. Fleming is waiting.

111
00:06:47.678 --> 00:06:49.313
Oh, wasn't the meeting
set for 9?

112
00:06:49.445 --> 00:06:52.215
Yes, 9 a.m. is when
the meeting starts,

113
00:06:52.349 --> 00:06:54.785
which is exactly now.

114
00:06:54.918 --> 00:06:57.254
Have you ever spent time
with him? Mr. Brok?

115
00:06:57.387 --> 00:06:58.487
No, of course not.

116
00:06:58.622 --> 00:06:59.990
He had me over
to his château,

117
00:07:00.123 --> 00:07:01.525
which is in France.

118
00:07:01.658 --> 00:07:04.460
And we were sitting there,
and I'm asking him,

119
00:07:04.594 --> 00:07:08.899
I said, "Mr. Brok, have you
ever heard of Humphry Davy?"

120
00:07:09.032 --> 00:07:10.434
- And he says, "No."
- Oh.

121
00:07:10.567 --> 00:07:12.903
I say, "Have you ever
heard of Joseph Swan

122
00:07:13.036 --> 00:07:15.806
or Alexander Lodygin?"
"No clue."

123
00:07:15.939 --> 00:07:17.407
So I say, "Okay.

124
00:07:17.541 --> 00:07:20.143
Uh, what about
Thomas Edison?"

125
00:07:20.277 --> 00:07:23.313
"Well, of course. Who hasn't?
He invented the light bulb."

126
00:07:23.447 --> 00:07:25.148
- Right? But guess what?
- Uh...

127
00:07:25.282 --> 00:07:27.117
So did those
other three guys.

128
00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.852
Before Edison.

129
00:07:28.986 --> 00:07:31.655
But Edison
was first to market.

130
00:07:31.788 --> 00:07:33.890
Do you see my point?

131
00:07:34.024 --> 00:07:35.993
We have a product that will

132
00:07:36.126 --> 00:07:38.662
revolutionize
the power industry.

133
00:07:38.795 --> 00:07:40.464
But we have to be first.

134
00:07:40.597 --> 00:07:42.199
The time is now.

135
00:07:42.332 --> 00:07:46.169
And that's what I told Mr. Brok,
and he agrees with me.

136
00:07:46.303 --> 00:07:47.871
Obviously.

137
00:07:48.005 --> 00:07:50.173
- I...
- Elena, thank you for coming in.

138
00:07:50.307 --> 00:07:51.842
I love how
this conversation went.

139
00:07:51.975 --> 00:07:53.777
Technically, I haven't
said anything.

140
00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.146
Let's not get caught in
a game of who said what.

141
00:07:56.279 --> 00:07:58.648
Mr. Fleming, I know how
important Calisto is, okay?

142
00:07:58.782 --> 00:08:00.851
I'm the lead programmer on it.
It's my baby.

143
00:08:00.984 --> 00:08:02.552
- Yeah.
- But as I wrote in my report,

144
00:08:02.686 --> 00:08:04.087
right now
there is a possibility

145
00:08:04.221 --> 00:08:06.356
for the harmonic range
to be reversed.

146
00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.392
We both know how dangerous
that could be.

147
00:08:08.525 --> 00:08:11.228
Well, I mean, you don't know
what I know. Heh.

148
00:08:11.361 --> 00:08:13.497
Y-you know Julio?
The second engineer?

149
00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.266
He's actually still in hospital
after a brain seizure,

150
00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.668
and he was only partially
exposed during a test.

151
00:08:18.802 --> 00:08:20.505
Allegedly. Allegedly.

152
00:08:20.637 --> 00:08:23.173
And Julio was an idiot.

153
00:08:23.306 --> 00:08:24.875
All I need is root access

154
00:08:25.008 --> 00:08:26.676
and time
to permanently fix the flaw

155
00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.645
in the blockchain
so it will stay safe...

156
00:08:30.113 --> 00:08:32.482
Ingrid,
can I get a cappuccino?

157
00:08:32.616 --> 00:08:34.551
Okay. I read your report.

158
00:08:34.684 --> 00:08:38.355
I've had others
read your report.

159
00:08:38.488 --> 00:08:40.557
We just simply
disagree with you.

160
00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:43.528
Has Mr. Brok read my report?
I think that if he read...

161
00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:46.663
Let me be crystal clear here.

162
00:08:46.797 --> 00:08:48.865
We have developed Calisto
for five years,

163
00:08:48.999 --> 00:08:50.734
and we are going to market.

164
00:08:50.867 --> 00:08:53.036
It is safe and it is ready,

165
00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.105
and that's what
we're telling Mr. Brok.

166
00:08:55.238 --> 00:08:58.909
And you are telling
Mr. Brok nothing.

167
00:09:01.611 --> 00:09:04.481
Look, Elena,
you're much too smart

168
00:09:04.614 --> 00:09:06.983
to keep pushing
this forward, aren't you?

169
00:09:10.887 --> 00:09:12.589
Good.

170
00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.666
- I knew who Humphry Davy was.
- Good for you.

171
00:09:28.939 --> 00:09:31.576
- You dropped something.
- Oh, no. That's not mine.

172
00:09:31.708 --> 00:09:34.711
Well, I don't litter,
so it must be yours.

173
00:09:36.581 --> 00:09:38.281
You might need it.

174
00:10:07.244 --> 00:10:08.678
Bosley, 001.

175
00:10:23.326 --> 00:10:25.662
You old codger.
You really thought

176
00:10:25.795 --> 00:10:28.999
we were gonna let you
just sneak away quietly?

177
00:10:29.132 --> 00:10:30.568
You didn't have to.

178
00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.935
It's not just me.

179
00:10:33.336 --> 00:10:35.705
<i>Surprise!</i>

180
00:10:35.839 --> 00:10:38.008
Surprise!

181
00:10:38.141 --> 00:10:40.810
- Hey! Bonjour.
- <i>Buenos días, señor.</i>

182
00:10:40.944 --> 00:10:43.113
- <i>Buenos días.</i>
- Gang's all here.

183
00:10:43.246 --> 00:10:46.116
We all wanted to wish you
a happy retirement.

184
00:10:46.249 --> 00:10:47.384
Thank you, Bosley.

185
00:10:47.518 --> 00:10:48.485
- And you, sir.
- Bosley.

186
00:10:48.619 --> 00:10:50.387
Bosley. Thank you.

187
00:10:50.521 --> 00:10:52.189
- You!
- You've had one hell of a run.

188
00:10:52.322 --> 00:10:53.790
It deserves to be celebrated.

189
00:10:53.924 --> 00:10:56.293
I even put together
a little walk down memory lane.

190
00:10:56.426 --> 00:10:57.961
- Shall we? Ha, ha!
- Oh, no, no.

191
00:10:58.094 --> 00:10:59.963
Here it comes.

192
00:11:00.096 --> 00:11:02.165
Oh, yeah! Ha, ha!

193
00:11:02.299 --> 00:11:04.868
- Fresh-faced Oxford graduate.
- Yeah!

194
00:11:05.001 --> 00:11:07.170
- Oh, Lord.
- I dug deep. Look at that.

195
00:11:07.304 --> 00:11:08.838
That's not a disguise.

196
00:11:08.972 --> 00:11:11.208
You clearly had a
lot of fun over the years.

197
00:11:11.341 --> 00:11:13.343
You know,
life was good in those days.

198
00:11:13.476 --> 00:11:14.945
Where did you get that suit?

199
00:11:15.078 --> 00:11:16.346
Monte Carlo.

200
00:11:16.479 --> 00:11:18.215
It really happened.
There's the proof.

201
00:11:20.317 --> 00:11:22.819
Well, when you opened
the European offices,

202
00:11:22.953 --> 00:11:25.188
you took the Townsend Agency
international.

203
00:11:25.322 --> 00:11:27.625
None of us would be here
without you.

204
00:11:27.757 --> 00:11:30.060
- Yes.
- Especially me. Thank you.

205
00:11:30.193 --> 00:11:34.097
Well, I'm very touched.
Thank you. All of you.

206
00:11:34.231 --> 00:11:36.534
<i>Say a few words. Come on,
speech, Bosley. Speech!</i>

207
00:11:36.667 --> 00:11:38.935
- Oh, no.
- <i>Speech, speech, speech!</i>

208
00:11:39.069 --> 00:11:41.706
<i>Speech, speech, speech!</i>

209
00:11:41.838 --> 00:11:42.906
Uh...

210
00:11:44.307 --> 00:11:47.043
Well, frankly,
I am overwhelmed.

211
00:11:49.312 --> 00:11:51.515
I'm grateful...

212
00:11:51.649 --> 00:11:55.118
for all the work
that we have done together.

213
00:11:55.252 --> 00:11:57.954
And, you know,
Charlie wasn't sure

214
00:11:58.088 --> 00:11:59.889
that we could replicate
the success

215
00:12:00.023 --> 00:12:02.192
that he had
here in California.

216
00:12:02.325 --> 00:12:04.227
- But we made it work...
- That's right.

217
00:12:04.361 --> 00:12:08.999
...in a world that was
really not ready for the Angels.

218
00:12:09.132 --> 00:12:11.301
For 40 years,

219
00:12:11.434 --> 00:12:13.504
I recruited them,
I trained them...

220
00:12:14.739 --> 00:12:16.439
and I'm so very proud
of them.

221
00:12:17.941 --> 00:12:19.510
Bosleys...

222
00:12:19.644 --> 00:12:21.746
- you keep them safe.
- Will do.

223
00:12:21.878 --> 00:12:23.980
- Hear, hear.
- <i>We will, my friend.</i>

224
00:12:24.114 --> 00:12:27.317
And so for me,
as Charlie said,

225
00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.486
time to make
an exit stage left.

226
00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.255
Wha... Ah,
speaking of Charlie...

227
00:12:33.456 --> 00:12:34.858
<i>Hello, Bosley.</i>

228
00:12:34.991 --> 00:12:36.493
Hello, Charlie.

229
00:12:36.627 --> 00:12:38.962
<i>If you look around this room,
old friend,</i>

230
00:12:39.095 --> 00:12:40.497
<i>you'll see the men and women</i>

231
00:12:40.631 --> 00:12:43.266
<i>who will carry your legacy
into the future.</i>

232
00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:47.070
<i>Your leadership and commitment
is unparalleled.</i>

233
00:12:47.203 --> 00:12:49.906
<i>We owe you a debt
we cannot repay.</i>

234
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.142
<i>So instead,
we got you a watch.</i>

235
00:12:53.711 --> 00:12:55.345
- A watch?
- Yes.

236
00:12:56.647 --> 00:12:59.115
- Oh!
- Thank you, Charlie.

237
00:12:59.249 --> 00:13:01.519
<i>Enjoy your retirement.</i>

238
00:13:01.652 --> 00:13:03.186
<i>You deserve it.</i>

239
00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.488
A toast!

240
00:13:05.623 --> 00:13:07.490
You really like to party.

241
00:13:07.625 --> 00:13:10.226
It's the day drinking.
That's what I like the most.

242
00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.995
You're not bad either.

243
00:13:12.128 --> 00:13:13.798
<i>To Bosley.</i>

244
00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.032
- To Bosley!
- To all of you.

245
00:13:25.475 --> 00:13:29.012
♪ This speech is my recital
I think it's very vital ♪

246
00:13:29.145 --> 00:13:32.015
♪ To rock a rhyme, that's right
On time, "It's Tricky" is... ♪

247
00:13:32.148 --> 00:13:34.384
Thank you. That's it.
Please move. He's coming.

248
00:13:34.518 --> 00:13:36.554
- For sure.
- Are we ready? Thank you.

249
00:13:36.687 --> 00:13:38.054
That was a sick flow,
bro.

250
00:13:38.188 --> 00:13:40.323
- Oh, shut up, shut up.
- You really went for it.

251
00:13:40.457 --> 00:13:41.692
There's two seats over there.

252
00:13:41.826 --> 00:13:42.992
- ♪ It's tricky ♪
- ♪ Tricky ♪

253
00:13:43.126 --> 00:13:44.060
- ♪ Tricky ♪
- ♪ Tricky ♪

254
00:13:44.194 --> 00:13:45.895
Langston, shut up.

255
00:13:46.029 --> 00:13:50.200
Everyone, please help me
welcome our founder,

256
00:13:50.333 --> 00:13:53.136
our benefactor,
Alexander Brok.

257
00:13:57.207 --> 00:13:58.843
Mr. Brok, you have set

258
00:13:58.975 --> 00:14:02.312
the highest standards
for innovation.

259
00:14:02.445 --> 00:14:05.181
I believe that I, along
with a little help from my team,

260
00:14:05.315 --> 00:14:08.151
have met that challenge.

261
00:14:08.284 --> 00:14:11.622
Today, I instructed
the Hamburg power utility

262
00:14:11.756 --> 00:14:15.760
to disconnect this building
from the electrical grid.

263
00:14:15.892 --> 00:14:19.429
But we are far from
powerless.

264
00:14:22.232 --> 00:14:23.433
Mr. Brok,

265
00:14:23.567 --> 00:14:25.703
would you grant us
root access?

266
00:14:27.203 --> 00:14:29.272
<i>Hello, Alexander.</i>

267
00:14:29.406 --> 00:14:31.074
<i>Root access granted.</i>

268
00:14:31.207 --> 00:14:33.878
Calisto,
turn on the lights.

269
00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:38.381
Calisto, pair
with sister devices.

270
00:14:41.017 --> 00:14:43.086
Calisto, full power.

271
00:14:50.861 --> 00:14:53.062
Brok Industries
can power the world.

272
00:14:59.837 --> 00:15:02.972
So you went with
rare-earth magnetics in the end?

273
00:15:03.106 --> 00:15:04.073
Ah, yes.

274
00:15:04.207 --> 00:15:06.276
Inside a cyanide
crystal matrix.

275
00:15:07.745 --> 00:15:10.581
- It's kyanite, but...
- Kyanite.

276
00:15:10.714 --> 00:15:12.783
- Um, may I?
- Please.

277
00:15:12.917 --> 00:15:14.852
You delivered on
the safety protocols?

278
00:15:14.984 --> 00:15:19.122
Oh, absolutely. Calisto only
talks with electrical circuitry.

279
00:15:19.255 --> 00:15:22.192
The current never touches
people, pets, plants.

280
00:15:22.325 --> 00:15:24.294
It's smart, and it's safe.

281
00:15:24.427 --> 00:15:26.797
Although, uh, in the spirit
of full disclosure,

282
00:15:26.931 --> 00:15:29.834
I should mention
one small thing.

283
00:15:29.966 --> 00:15:33.604
It can be manufactured
in pastel colors for the ladies.

284
00:15:37.474 --> 00:15:38.676
You...

285
00:15:38.809 --> 00:15:42.847
Ah, well, this is it.

286
00:15:44.447 --> 00:15:47.150
We can bring clean energy
to everyone.

287
00:15:47.918 --> 00:15:49.185
Sustainably.

288
00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:53.490
Calisto is the future.

289
00:15:53.624 --> 00:15:56.794
And I am holding the future
in my hands, finally.

290
00:15:58.127 --> 00:15:59.697
Good work, guys.

291
00:16:00.798 --> 00:16:02.465
Good work.

292
00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.702
Come on, let's celebrate.
Drinks in the bar!

293
00:16:08.572 --> 00:16:11.274
Keep your form. Block.

294
00:16:11.407 --> 00:16:12.475
One, two.

295
00:16:16.145 --> 00:16:18.014
Let's take this one off.
Make it tighter.

296
00:16:18.147 --> 00:16:19.683
Okay.

297
00:16:22.553 --> 00:16:23.821
Thanks.

298
00:16:23.954 --> 00:16:26.222
Paris is not so bad, right?

299
00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:28.916
Did you take the apartment
with the good light?

300
00:16:28.993 --> 00:16:31.127
Yes. But if you get me a plant...

301
00:16:31.189 --> 00:16:32.596
- I'm just gonna kill it.
- Of course.

302
00:16:33.898 --> 00:16:34.765
<i>D'accord, d'accord.</i>

303
00:16:34.899 --> 00:16:36.534
I'm ready for a new assignment.

304
00:16:36.667 --> 00:16:39.770
Listen,
I've set a meeting with a new client.

305
00:16:39.904 --> 00:16:42.171
A corporate whistle-blower.

306
00:16:42.305 --> 00:16:44.207
Putting a team together.

307
00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.876
- A... A team?
- Yes.

308
00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:47.711
Hey, Bosley.

309
00:16:47.845 --> 00:16:50.346
- You wanted to see me, right?
- Ah, yes.

310
00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:51.414
Oh, hey.

311
00:16:51.549 --> 00:16:55.218
You're the former
MI6 ninja.

312
00:16:55.351 --> 00:16:56.319
Is it June?

313
00:16:56.452 --> 00:16:57.721
Oh, Jane.

314
00:16:57.855 --> 00:17:00.390
Oh, Jane. Jane.
Not the month.

315
00:17:00.524 --> 00:17:01.491
Sabrina?

316
00:17:01.625 --> 00:17:03.561
Sabina. It's Italian.

317
00:17:03.694 --> 00:17:05.663
Oh, are you Italian?

318
00:17:05.796 --> 00:17:07.363
No. I... Maybe...

319
00:17:07.497 --> 00:17:10.099
We have a situation in Hamburg,
a new client.

320
00:17:10.233 --> 00:17:13.504
Hamburg. Interestingly, not
where hamburgers were invented.

321
00:17:13.637 --> 00:17:14.939
That was in Frankfurt,

322
00:17:15.071 --> 00:17:17.140
where frankfurters were
not invented, which...

323
00:17:17.273 --> 00:17:20.109
- I don't think that this is...
- I'm sorry. I'm vegetarian.

324
00:17:20.243 --> 00:17:22.412
Thank you very much.
But I recall hearing

325
00:17:22.546 --> 00:17:24.380
you two worked
well together in Rio.

326
00:17:24.515 --> 00:17:26.884
I recall her
pushing me off a roof.

327
00:17:27.017 --> 00:17:28.986
I recall
it was time to go.

328
00:17:29.118 --> 00:17:31.722
Heh. That makes sense.

329
00:17:31.855 --> 00:17:33.657
Who's the client?

330
00:17:36.026 --> 00:17:37.061
Follow me.

331
00:18:11.127 --> 00:18:12.462
- Elena?
- Hi.

332
00:18:12.596 --> 00:18:13.897
Welcome.

333
00:18:14.031 --> 00:18:15.331
Uh, Mr. Bosley?

334
00:18:15.465 --> 00:18:18.669
- Just Bosley.
- Thank you for seeing me. Um...

335
00:18:21.137 --> 00:18:24.173
- Would you like anything?
- Uh, espresso, <i>bitte.</i>

336
00:18:24.307 --> 00:18:25.843
<i>Merci, ça va.</i>

337
00:18:27.978 --> 00:18:29.379
Espresso.

338
00:18:29.513 --> 00:18:31.015
COS perimeter check.

339
00:18:31.147 --> 00:18:32.616
"COS"?

340
00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.985
I have less than no idea
what that means,

341
00:18:35.119 --> 00:18:38.022
but you are good up here.

342
00:18:38.154 --> 00:18:39.657
I would say,

343
00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.491
the coast is clear.

344
00:18:41.625 --> 00:18:43.459
<i>Yes, exactly.</i>

345
00:18:43.594 --> 00:18:45.062
I have thought
about this a lot.

346
00:18:45.194 --> 00:18:47.031
All we have to do
is get it to Mr. Brok.

347
00:18:47.163 --> 00:18:49.066
<i>And I have tried
to contact him.</i>

348
00:18:49.198 --> 00:18:52.002
Well, it takes a lot
to come forward,

349
00:18:52.136 --> 00:18:54.705
and I appreciate
your courage.

350
00:18:54.838 --> 00:18:57.007
You sure you wanna
take this risk?

351
00:18:58.408 --> 00:19:00.010
Yeah.

352
00:19:00.144 --> 00:19:02.112
Okay, we can help you.

353
00:19:02.245 --> 00:19:05.115
- It's just getting out of hand.
- Stop it, you're so cute.

354
00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:07.785
I gotta get a dog.

355
00:19:09.086 --> 00:19:10.921
<i>I can't sleep at night,</i>

356
00:19:11.055 --> 00:19:14.558
<i>knowing and not being allowed
to do or say anything about it.</i>

357
00:19:17.427 --> 00:19:18.729
I can fix it,

358
00:19:18.862 --> 00:19:21.065
but I just need
the opportunity.

359
00:19:21.197 --> 00:19:24.333
I believe you. Were you able
to get the evidence?

360
00:19:27.871 --> 00:19:29.506
All my reports, all my data.

361
00:19:43.137 --> 00:19:44.567
What can I bring you?

362
00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.869
Your check, sir.

363
00:19:59.002 --> 00:20:00.436
Was that the signal?

364
00:20:00.571 --> 00:20:02.438
- Elena...
- <i>What's happening?</i>

365
00:20:02.573 --> 00:20:04.174
You need to go
to the ladies' room.

366
00:20:04.307 --> 00:20:06.844
- No, I'm fine. Thank you.
- Quickly.

367
00:20:09.213 --> 00:20:11.081
<i>Hey, what's happening? Jane?</i>

368
00:20:11.215 --> 00:20:12.516
Now!

369
00:20:14.383 --> 00:20:16.385
Hello... Oh, shit!

370
00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.755
Shit!

371
00:20:22.926 --> 00:20:26.262
Ah! Shit, shit, shit!

372
00:21:19.382 --> 00:21:20.517
That's my gun.

373
00:21:27.124 --> 00:21:28.992
Sabina! Hurry!

374
00:21:29.126 --> 00:21:30.027
- Go!
- Go!

375
00:21:32.529 --> 00:21:35.364
Yeah! Evac the client!
That's what I was gonna say!

376
00:21:35.498 --> 00:21:36.900
Whoa!

377
00:21:40.804 --> 00:21:41.905
What's going on?

378
00:21:42.039 --> 00:21:44.541
- Oh, God. You're not a waitress?
- No.

379
00:21:44.675 --> 00:21:47.511
I'm Jane. Nice to meet you.

380
00:21:47.644 --> 00:21:49.880
- Did you bring the big gun?
- In the back.

381
00:21:50.013 --> 00:21:52.683
- Can you move your feet?
- Oh, sure. Mm-hm.

382
00:21:52.816 --> 00:21:54.551
Oh, do you know how
to use that?

383
00:22:01.625 --> 00:22:02.826
Motherfucker!

384
00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:05.361
Oh, my God!
Is he shooting at us?!

385
00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:12.169
- Hold on, ladies.
- Whoa!

386
00:22:16.840 --> 00:22:17.975
Whoa!

387
00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:27.084
Is that a tank? Oh, my God.
Where'd he go? Where'd he go?

388
00:22:27.217 --> 00:22:29.720
- I think we lost him!
- Bit much for just this girl, no?

389
00:22:29.853 --> 00:22:30.921
Who is this chick?

390
00:22:31.054 --> 00:22:32.022
Who am I?!

391
00:22:32.155 --> 00:22:33.389
Who are you?! Who is he?

392
00:22:33.523 --> 00:22:35.225
And why is he
shooting at us?

393
00:22:35.359 --> 00:22:36.459
Keep it steady.

394
00:22:36.593 --> 00:22:38.128
Oh, my God. I'm gonna die.

395
00:22:41.031 --> 00:22:42.099
Oh, no! He's back!

396
00:23:06.223 --> 00:23:07.257
Oh, my God!

397
00:23:12.362 --> 00:23:13.363
Oh, shit!

398
00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:20.971
<i>Merde!</i>

399
00:23:34.217 --> 00:23:35.451
Stay low. Stay low.

400
00:23:40.489 --> 00:23:43.293
- Do a J-turn on my mark.
- Ready.

401
00:23:43.427 --> 00:23:44.761
Now!

402
00:24:01.578 --> 00:24:03.113
Bosley.

403
00:25:08.678 --> 00:25:10.047
Stay down!

404
00:25:12.616 --> 00:25:13.550
Jane!

405
00:25:15.786 --> 00:25:17.522
Hey, I said, stay down!

406
00:25:17.687 --> 00:25:19.156
Hey! Stop moving!

407
00:25:58.962 --> 00:26:00.831
Sandwich?

408
00:26:00.964 --> 00:26:02.466
It's tuna.

409
00:26:02.599 --> 00:26:05.769
Unless it's cheese,
and it's not good.

410
00:26:13.578 --> 00:26:15.612
How about you?
You hungry?

411
00:26:39.269 --> 00:26:40.837
Charlie sends love, Angels.

412
00:26:40.971 --> 00:26:44.274
Who is she?
Who is she?

413
00:26:44.407 --> 00:26:47.043
Hey, she's in shock,
and she smells like puke.

414
00:26:47.177 --> 00:26:48.178
Who are you?

415
00:26:48.311 --> 00:26:50.647
- I'm Bosley.
- Bosley?

416
00:26:50.780 --> 00:26:52.883
Bosley's a rank
in our organization.

417
00:26:53.016 --> 00:26:55.652
It's like a lieutenant.

418
00:26:55.785 --> 00:26:58.488
The real name of the man
you met was Edgar Dessange.

419
00:27:00.257 --> 00:27:01.725
Edgar.

420
00:27:05.929 --> 00:27:08.031
Jane, I'm really sorry.

421
00:27:08.165 --> 00:27:11.101
- I know how much he meant to you.
- Oh, I don't need a hug.

422
00:27:13.770 --> 00:27:15.772
Well, I do.

423
00:27:15.906 --> 00:27:17.608
He was my friend too.

424
00:27:22.846 --> 00:27:24.281
Hugs work.

425
00:27:29.252 --> 00:27:31.488
Okay, let's get you
cleaned up.

426
00:27:31.622 --> 00:27:33.023
Come on.

427
00:27:33.156 --> 00:27:34.559
Is that a stolen car?

428
00:27:35.859 --> 00:27:36.860
Okay.

429
00:27:38.161 --> 00:27:40.864
Bosley, 342.
Open Safe House 6.

430
00:27:47.804 --> 00:27:50.541
Boz, who else knew we were
meeting with Elena in Hamburg?

431
00:27:50.675 --> 00:27:53.176
Well, protocol would
be not to tell anyone.

432
00:27:53.310 --> 00:27:54.945
Why do you ask?

433
00:27:55.078 --> 00:27:56.746
Well, Bosley...

434
00:27:56.880 --> 00:27:59.115
Edgar thought...

435
00:28:01.151 --> 00:28:02.919
Okay, you didn't see
this guy.

436
00:28:03.053 --> 00:28:05.255
He was a pro, and he brought
a lot of firepower

437
00:28:05.388 --> 00:28:06.524
for such an easy target.

438
00:28:06.657 --> 00:28:08.258
Yeah, he was so extra, right?

439
00:28:08.391 --> 00:28:10.460
I could take that girl out
with a flyswatter.

440
00:28:10.595 --> 00:28:12.862
He rocks up in this
urban assault vehicle.

441
00:28:12.996 --> 00:28:15.566
So we're thinking what?
He was...

442
00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:18.401
Maybe she was
being watched...

443
00:28:18.536 --> 00:28:19.869
but what if we are?

444
00:28:20.003 --> 00:28:23.608
- And by who?
- Hey, you guys. All cleaned up.

445
00:28:23.740 --> 00:28:26.677
- Feeling better?
- Yes, thank you.

446
00:28:26.810 --> 00:28:29.112
I'm kind of getting this,
you know.

447
00:28:29.246 --> 00:28:32.115
You guys are
like lady spies and...

448
00:28:32.249 --> 00:28:34.751
I just need you to explain
who this guy is

449
00:28:34.884 --> 00:28:37.787
- and why was he shooting at you.
- Oh, you.

450
00:28:37.921 --> 00:28:40.524
- He was shooting at you.
- Jane.

451
00:28:42.092 --> 00:28:43.827
At me?

452
00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:45.495
- Oh, God.
- Hey.

453
00:28:45.630 --> 00:28:47.632
- Okay.
- Just have some tea.

454
00:28:47.764 --> 00:28:50.400
The shooter's a ghost.
Facial recognition's popped him

455
00:28:50.534 --> 00:28:54.672
in a few places over the years
but no name, no record, nothing.

456
00:28:54.804 --> 00:28:56.473
He's got friends
in high places.

457
00:28:56.607 --> 00:28:59.476
- I'm gonna kill him.
- I'm obliged to remind you,

458
00:28:59.610 --> 00:29:01.579
Charlie frowns on revenge,
Jane.

459
00:29:01.712 --> 00:29:03.813
So, Ms. Houghlin,

460
00:29:03.947 --> 00:29:07.917
your file says you are a systems
engineer on the Calisto project.

461
00:29:08.051 --> 00:29:09.953
Uh, you know about Calisto?

462
00:29:10.086 --> 00:29:12.222
We know about
a lot of things.

463
00:29:12.355 --> 00:29:14.791
That you graduated top
of your class at MIT,

464
00:29:14.924 --> 00:29:17.127
you take Krav Maga,
you ride your bike to work.

465
00:29:17.260 --> 00:29:18.995
You think yellow
is one of your colors

466
00:29:19.129 --> 00:29:20.230
when, in fact,
it's no one's.

467
00:29:20.363 --> 00:29:22.165
That you could be dating more

468
00:29:22.299 --> 00:29:25.402
if you played up the cheekbones
in your online profile pictures.

469
00:29:25.536 --> 00:29:29.105
What we don't know is
why someone wants you dead.

470
00:29:29.239 --> 00:29:31.341
<i>I know it can be fixed.</i>

471
00:29:31.474 --> 00:29:34.010
<i>Let's take this
one step at a time.</i>

472
00:29:34.144 --> 00:29:36.146
<i>There's a flaw in the system.</i>

473
00:29:36.279 --> 00:29:37.615
What's the flaw?

474
00:29:38.915 --> 00:29:40.183
Calisto can be weaponized.

475
00:29:41.918 --> 00:29:43.820
I mean, I can fix it.
But right now,

476
00:29:43.953 --> 00:29:46.122
any decent hacker,
curious or criminal enough,

477
00:29:46.256 --> 00:29:49.660
could turn Calisto into an EMP
on the human body.

478
00:29:49.794 --> 00:29:51.294
An electromagnetic pulse.

479
00:29:51.428 --> 00:29:52.797
A brain seizure,
essentially.

480
00:29:52.929 --> 00:29:54.831
- Yes.
- See? I know stuff.

481
00:29:54.964 --> 00:29:56.667
It disrupts
the neural networks

482
00:29:56.801 --> 00:29:58.736
and looks like
a stroke or an aneurysm.

483
00:29:58.868 --> 00:30:01.204
So it can be used
without a trace of evidence.

484
00:30:01.338 --> 00:30:03.306
A perfect
assassination machine.

485
00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:05.543
Yeah.
And it can be triggered remotely

486
00:30:05.676 --> 00:30:08.579
across the network
that I created.

487
00:30:08.713 --> 00:30:10.347
Dope. See, that
is what you can do

488
00:30:10.480 --> 00:30:12.982
- if you pay attention in school.
- Who knows about this?

489
00:30:13.116 --> 00:30:16.353
I filed a report after
it almost killed my colleague

490
00:30:16.486 --> 00:30:19.724
during a security test,
but I think it was buried.

491
00:30:19.856 --> 00:30:21.726
My report,
not my colleague. No.

492
00:30:21.858 --> 00:30:23.561
Julio is fine. He, uh...

493
00:30:23.694 --> 00:30:25.730
He just can't speak
or see color anymore.

494
00:30:25.862 --> 00:30:27.364
It's not in production yet?

495
00:30:27.497 --> 00:30:30.634
No, we're behind schedule,
but there are six prototypes

496
00:30:30.768 --> 00:30:33.069
in the Brok facility vault,
plus the one at my lab

497
00:30:33.203 --> 00:30:35.238
that I was using
to program the fix, which...

498
00:30:35.372 --> 00:30:37.207
Let's get those prototypes
out of there.

499
00:30:37.340 --> 00:30:40.644
Uh, I'm sorry. Can we just
hit pause for a second, please?

500
00:30:40.778 --> 00:30:42.212
Does your company
have a website

501
00:30:42.345 --> 00:30:44.147
with an employee directory
with photos?

502
00:30:44.280 --> 00:30:47.050
Yes, but Brok Industries is
equipped with insane security.

503
00:30:47.183 --> 00:30:48.719
- There's no way...
- There we go.

504
00:30:48.853 --> 00:30:51.020
Do you think she still has
security clearance?

505
00:30:51.154 --> 00:30:52.489
If she doesn't,
we'll know

506
00:30:52.623 --> 00:30:54.725
the threat comes from within,
so either way...

507
00:30:54.859 --> 00:30:58.061
- We get the information we need.
- No, no, no.

508
00:30:58.194 --> 00:30:59.929
No, no.

509
00:31:00.063 --> 00:31:02.198
- Ooh!
- No.

510
00:31:02.332 --> 00:31:04.467
- No, no, no.
- I...

511
00:31:04.602 --> 00:31:06.136
Huh. Hm...

512
00:31:06.269 --> 00:31:08.972
- Bowl cuts.
- Bowl cuts.

513
00:31:09.105 --> 00:31:10.273
Bowl cuts.

514
00:31:12.510 --> 00:31:13.644
Bowl cuts.

515
00:31:29.058 --> 00:31:30.694
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah.

516
00:31:30.828 --> 00:31:32.462
Just trying
to get to work, Ralph.

517
00:31:32.596 --> 00:31:35.432
Well, I gotta do my job too.

518
00:31:36.700 --> 00:31:37.735
Okay.

519
00:31:40.370 --> 00:31:42.939
- New look, huh?
- Mm-hm.

520
00:31:43.072 --> 00:31:45.609
I like it a lot.

521
00:31:45.743 --> 00:31:48.278
Aren't you holding
people up, Ralph?

522
00:31:48.411 --> 00:31:50.413
Well...

523
00:31:50.548 --> 00:31:52.315
you have yourself
a good day.

524
00:31:52.449 --> 00:31:54.652
And don't... Don't forget
to smile, yeah?

525
00:32:27.317 --> 00:32:28.418
What?

526
00:32:30.921 --> 00:32:33.691
How...? How did you
even get in the...?

527
00:32:33.824 --> 00:32:36.594
Oh, God. What did
you do to Pradeep?

528
00:32:36.727 --> 00:32:37.994
Pradeep Prasad.

529
00:32:38.127 --> 00:32:40.363
<i>Nothing. Pradeep's fine.</i>

530
00:32:42.967 --> 00:32:46.269
<i>I nabbed his ID card
from the gym this morning.</i>

531
00:32:46.402 --> 00:32:48.104
Hi.

532
00:32:48.238 --> 00:32:50.039
Bye.

533
00:32:50.173 --> 00:32:52.242
- Hi.
- Hi.

534
00:32:54.310 --> 00:32:56.079
And Sven?

535
00:32:56.212 --> 00:32:57.581
<i>I compressed his carotid</i>

536
00:32:57.715 --> 00:32:59.550
<i>and deoxygenated
his brain stem.</i>

537
00:33:00.651 --> 00:33:01.752
<i>What?</i>

538
00:33:01.886 --> 00:33:03.721
Well, that sounds painful.

539
00:33:03.854 --> 00:33:05.355
Yeah, it's like
taking a nap.

540
00:33:05.488 --> 00:33:08.391
You smell burnt toast,
then everything goes dark.

541
00:33:08.526 --> 00:33:10.393
Hey, don't worry,
he's gonna wake up.

542
00:33:10.528 --> 00:33:12.095
Heh, unless he doesn't.

543
00:33:12.228 --> 00:33:13.898
- What...?
- We should go.

544
00:33:14.030 --> 00:33:16.366
If we're in the building
when they do their sweep,

545
00:33:16.499 --> 00:33:17.868
we're going
to German prison.

546
00:33:18.002 --> 00:33:19.937
Hm, and then it's schnitzel.
All the time.

547
00:33:20.069 --> 00:33:21.505
Not such a bad deal,
actually.

548
00:33:21.639 --> 00:33:23.641
Sabina, you get Calisto
from the vault.

549
00:33:23.774 --> 00:33:25.809
Elena, you get the prototype
from your lab.

550
00:33:25.943 --> 00:33:27.511
I'll keep security
distracted.

551
00:33:27.645 --> 00:33:30.046
Okay. You ready?

552
00:33:30.179 --> 00:33:32.148
Yeah. High five.
Girl power.

553
00:33:37.220 --> 00:33:38.889
Oh.

554
00:33:39.023 --> 00:33:40.658
Thank you.

555
00:33:45.295 --> 00:33:46.664
No puking.

556
00:34:19.195 --> 00:34:20.631
Buggy piece of shit.

557
00:34:34.578 --> 00:34:36.647
Whoa... No.

558
00:34:38.281 --> 00:34:40.316
- Boz, you with us?
- I'm here. What do you got?

559
00:34:40.450 --> 00:34:42.418
Calisto's gone.
It's not here.

560
00:34:42.553 --> 00:34:43.787
<i>Someone beat us to it.</i>

561
00:34:43.921 --> 00:34:45.789
The plot thickens.
Can you get an ID?

562
00:34:51.962 --> 00:34:54.130
There we go. Some guy.
Peter Fleming.

563
00:34:54.263 --> 00:34:56.000
Let's see what Elena
comes back with.

564
00:34:58.301 --> 00:35:01.437
Hold up. We might have
another problem.

565
00:35:01.572 --> 00:35:03.841
Your boy Pradeep
just showed up.

566
00:35:03.974 --> 00:35:05.441
Pradeep didn't spin?

567
00:35:05.576 --> 00:35:07.811
But he signed up
for the Groupon and everything.

568
00:35:07.945 --> 00:35:09.178
Well, he's here.

569
00:35:13.851 --> 00:35:14.852
- Ralph?
- Yeah?

570
00:35:14.985 --> 00:35:16.352
We've got
Pradeep Prasad here.

571
00:35:16.486 --> 00:35:18.187
The system says
he's in the building.

572
00:35:18.321 --> 00:35:19.657
Yeah, there's a glitch.

573
00:35:19.790 --> 00:35:22.960
The computer
thinks Elena Houghlin is...

574
00:35:24.762 --> 00:35:27.497
Right now, I'm sending you
an image of Elena Houghlin.

575
00:35:27.631 --> 00:35:29.198
Get it to all our guys.
I want her

576
00:35:29.332 --> 00:35:31.167
- detained for questioning.
- Yes.

577
00:35:54.792 --> 00:35:57.027
She's in her lab.

578
00:35:57.161 --> 00:35:58.361
Let's go.

579
00:36:07.071 --> 00:36:08.906
And here comes
the cavalry.

580
00:36:10.140 --> 00:36:11.942
The heat is assembling,
ladies.

581
00:36:13.177 --> 00:36:15.378
Oh, they know.

582
00:36:15.512 --> 00:36:17.346
All right, meet me
at the pickup.

583
00:36:21.752 --> 00:36:23.754
Sabina?
This one's real hard.

584
00:36:23.887 --> 00:36:27.124
I need you to exhibit
some attention-seeking behavior.

585
00:36:28.826 --> 00:36:30.194
I have so many ideas.

586
00:36:34.898 --> 00:36:35.833
Houghlin?

587
00:36:37.901 --> 00:36:38.936
Where is she?

588
00:36:40.204 --> 00:36:41.705
- Where is she?
- I don't know.

589
00:36:41.839 --> 00:36:43.406
- Wait, wait, wait.
- What?

590
00:36:43.540 --> 00:36:44.875
- Now I got her.
- Where?

591
00:36:45.008 --> 00:36:46.176
Here.

592
00:36:47.310 --> 00:36:48.779
Eleven?

593
00:36:48.912 --> 00:36:51.380
Guys, she's on 11.
Level 11, women's restroom.

594
00:37:01.091 --> 00:37:02.760
Hi. Uh, who are you?

595
00:37:02.893 --> 00:37:05.062
Shh. Sit down.
Hands where I can see them.

596
00:37:10.801 --> 00:37:13.302
Are you with Health and Safety?

597
00:37:13.436 --> 00:37:15.906
God, these things
are impossible to open.

598
00:37:18.809 --> 00:37:23.080
Um, you're really not supposed
to be touching things in here

599
00:37:23.213 --> 00:37:25.949
unless you're supposed to be
touching things in here.

600
00:37:34.691 --> 00:37:37.227
You put your mouth on it.

601
00:37:37.360 --> 00:37:40.731
Twenty billion bacteria
reside in the human mouth.

602
00:37:42.266 --> 00:37:43.567
You're adorable.

603
00:37:44.935 --> 00:37:47.336
Jane?
Jane, is that you flirting?

604
00:37:59.216 --> 00:38:00.284
Hey!

605
00:38:01.417 --> 00:38:03.287
Stop! Hey!

606
00:38:04.655 --> 00:38:05.789
Hey!

607
00:38:38.255 --> 00:38:39.189
Oh, come on.

608
00:39:01.278 --> 00:39:02.346
You ready?

609
00:39:07.551 --> 00:39:09.286
Hey! Hey!

610
00:39:10.721 --> 00:39:12.455
- Sorry!
- Hey!

611
00:39:13.557 --> 00:39:15.458
Oh, my God!

612
00:39:15.592 --> 00:39:16.894
Get back here!

613
00:39:19.897 --> 00:39:20.864
Who has eyes on her?

614
00:39:20.998 --> 00:39:22.032
She set a fire on four.

615
00:39:22.165 --> 00:39:23.533
We are following her
to three.

616
00:39:23.667 --> 00:39:27.070
- Let's go, guys! Come on.
- Three? She was on 11.

617
00:39:28.238 --> 00:39:30.774
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

618
00:39:32.509 --> 00:39:34.278
What did you...?

619
00:39:34.410 --> 00:39:37.080
- Hold this.
- Okay.

620
00:39:37.214 --> 00:39:39.448
Oh, that's...
That's not you.

621
00:39:39.583 --> 00:39:40.951
No.

622
00:39:42.686 --> 00:39:45.022
- Hold this.
- Okay.

623
00:39:45.155 --> 00:39:47.224
Can you unzip me?

624
00:39:47.357 --> 00:39:48.859
Yeah, yeah. Uh...

625
00:39:50.227 --> 00:39:51.128
Sorry.

626
00:39:56.900 --> 00:39:58.802
Bye.

627
00:39:58.936 --> 00:40:00.871
- You don't want your...?
- Keep it!

628
00:40:25.295 --> 00:40:26.763
- <i>Hello?</i>
- Hey, Susan.

629
00:40:26.897 --> 00:40:29.199
Mr. Fleming would like you
in the lab right away.

630
00:40:29.333 --> 00:40:30.867
- <i>I'll be right there.</i>
- Okay. Thanks.

631
00:40:31.001 --> 00:40:32.970
- Did you see her?
- Yes.

632
00:40:33.103 --> 00:40:34.805
Not on-screen. With your eyes!

633
00:40:34.938 --> 00:40:36.873
- You go there, you go there. Now!
- Okay!

634
00:40:39.609 --> 00:40:40.777
<i>I'm out.</i>

635
00:40:40.911 --> 00:40:41.845
I'm out.

636
00:40:44.614 --> 00:40:47.150
- Main lobby. I see her!
- Where?!

637
00:40:48.452 --> 00:40:50.486
Lobby level.
Lobby level!

638
00:40:50.620 --> 00:40:52.889
Let's go, guys. Come on!

639
00:40:53.023 --> 00:40:54.958
Put your hands
where I can see them.

640
00:40:56.259 --> 00:40:57.627
Get on the ground! Now!

641
00:40:57.761 --> 00:40:58.996
Let me see your hands!

642
00:40:59.129 --> 00:41:00.530
- Do it!
- What for?

643
00:41:00.664 --> 00:41:02.332
I don't know.
I don't know! Ah!

644
00:41:02.466 --> 00:41:05.268
I don't know what for.
What are you looking for? Ah!

645
00:41:05.402 --> 00:41:06.703
Sorry, Susan.

646
00:41:11.541 --> 00:41:14.244
"Susan Olsen."

647
00:41:14.378 --> 00:41:18.081
Put all the exits on lockdown.
Sweep from the bottom up.

648
00:41:18.215 --> 00:41:19.850
Jane. I got it.

649
00:41:19.983 --> 00:41:22.519
The unit's gone. We need to go.
Someone beat us to it.

650
00:41:22.652 --> 00:41:24.388
Are you kidding?
They were stolen?

651
00:41:24.521 --> 00:41:26.223
- Oh, no, no, no!
- Oh!

652
00:41:26.356 --> 00:41:28.892
- Oh!
- God!

653
00:41:29.026 --> 00:41:30.994
Any ideas?
Is there another way out?

654
00:41:31.128 --> 00:41:33.263
Wait, wait. I can hack this.

655
00:41:33.397 --> 00:41:36.501
Turn it into an EMP, overload
the electronics in the door.

656
00:41:36.633 --> 00:41:38.268
Won't that kill us
in the process?

657
00:41:38.402 --> 00:41:41.506
It's short proximity. We should
be okay if we keep our distance.

658
00:41:41.638 --> 00:41:43.707
- How far?
- Uh...

659
00:41:43.840 --> 00:41:45.142
Here is far enough, I guess.

660
00:41:45.275 --> 00:41:47.044
You guess?
Do scientists usually guess?

661
00:41:47.177 --> 00:41:50.013
Of course. It's the first step
in the scientific method.

662
00:41:50.147 --> 00:41:52.315
Hypothesis.

663
00:41:52.449 --> 00:41:54.551
Calisto, short-range
power burst.

664
00:41:54.684 --> 00:41:56.753
Okay, it's powering up.
It's powering up.

665
00:42:01.358 --> 00:42:02.692
This should work.

666
00:42:07.497 --> 00:42:09.166
- Ralph.
- No.

667
00:42:09.299 --> 00:42:10.233
God.

668
00:42:13.270 --> 00:42:14.539
- I have time.
- No.

669
00:42:14.671 --> 00:42:17.741
- I have to. I have to.
- No. No. Stay here!

670
00:42:17.874 --> 00:42:20.377
Ralph? Ralph.
Get over here now.

671
00:42:20.511 --> 00:42:22.446
- There you are.
- Ralph, it's about to blow.

672
00:42:22.579 --> 00:42:24.714
I can't stop it.
Get over here.

673
00:42:24.848 --> 00:42:26.551
You think
I'm gonna listen to you?

674
00:42:26.683 --> 00:42:30.053
- Ralph, come! Get over here now!
- Put hands where I can see them!

675
00:42:43.433 --> 00:42:45.536
Let's get out of here.
Do we need that?

676
00:42:45.669 --> 00:42:47.404
- No, it's useless now.
- Then leave it.

677
00:42:47.538 --> 00:42:50.073
Move it or lose it, ladies.
Let's go. We gotta go.

678
00:42:50.207 --> 00:42:52.609
Come on, come on. Get in.

679
00:43:05.789 --> 00:43:07.724
Do you think
Ralph's gonna be okay?

680
00:43:09.059 --> 00:43:11.461
Oh, yeah.
I'm sure he's fine.

681
00:43:11.596 --> 00:43:13.663
- He seemed fine, right?
- Yeah.

682
00:43:13.797 --> 00:43:16.867
I'm sure... I'm sure he's okay.
I'm sure he's fine.

683
00:43:21.805 --> 00:43:25.008
Oh, well, that's a shame.

684
00:43:25.142 --> 00:43:27.477
Obviously, this is
a disappointing setback,

685
00:43:27.612 --> 00:43:30.280
but we have time.

686
00:43:30.413 --> 00:43:33.150
Do you know what?
Just get John on the phone.

687
00:43:33.283 --> 00:43:34.284
Now.

688
00:43:36.686 --> 00:43:38.855
Well, then wake him up.

689
00:43:43.793 --> 00:43:44.794
Everything all right?

690
00:43:47.497 --> 00:43:48.533
Can I have your phone?

691
00:44:28.639 --> 00:44:30.407
Bosley, 342.

692
00:44:46.022 --> 00:44:49.826
Welcome to the Berlin
outpost of the Townsend Agency.

693
00:44:49.960 --> 00:44:51.828
Is there food?
I'm starving.

694
00:44:51.962 --> 00:44:54.532
All women are starving
all the time.

695
00:44:57.367 --> 00:45:01.071
- <i>Mi chico.</i>
- Here they are. Welcome back.

696
00:45:01.204 --> 00:45:02.607
<i>Mi amor, como estas?</i>

697
00:45:02.739 --> 00:45:03.873
- Very <i>bien.</i>
- Good.

698
00:45:04.007 --> 00:45:05.775
- Cool.
- Well...

699
00:45:05.909 --> 00:45:07.511
Hey.

700
00:45:08.713 --> 00:45:10.581
You owe me a burpee now, okay?

701
00:45:12.215 --> 00:45:15.620
- Hey. Bombay sister. How are you?
- Master.

702
00:45:15.752 --> 00:45:17.220
Good to see you.

703
00:45:17.354 --> 00:45:19.055
- This is Elena.
- Pleasure to meet you.

704
00:45:19.189 --> 00:45:21.559
- Saint.
- Wow.

705
00:45:21.692 --> 00:45:24.928
Wow. You have
this beautiful energy.

706
00:45:25.061 --> 00:45:26.896
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

707
00:45:27.030 --> 00:45:29.399
- Oh, Jesus.
- Oh, wait, what?

708
00:45:29.533 --> 00:45:32.302
- Oh, my God. Yeah, um...
- Oh, no.

709
00:45:32.435 --> 00:45:35.573
I would love to apply
a firm touch to your back.

710
00:45:35.706 --> 00:45:37.941
- Do you consent?
- Yeah, sure.

711
00:45:38.074 --> 00:45:40.143
Okay. Just let me
try to find this.

712
00:45:41.478 --> 00:45:43.748
- Oh! Oh.
- Oh, yeah.

713
00:45:43.880 --> 00:45:44.848
- Oh.
- Good?

714
00:45:44.981 --> 00:45:46.584
Oh, yeah, yeah. Amazing.

715
00:45:46.717 --> 00:45:48.351
Displaced rib.
Very common.

716
00:45:48.485 --> 00:45:51.421
If you ever need additional
adjustments, I'm here for you.

717
00:45:51.555 --> 00:45:53.923
The Saint takes care
of our health and well-being.

718
00:45:54.057 --> 00:45:56.560
- Keeps us in fighting shape
- Yeah. Well, I try.

719
00:45:56.694 --> 00:45:59.095
He feeds our mind,
body and soul.

720
00:45:59.229 --> 00:46:02.132
Oh, should we take
a moment to remember Edgar?

721
00:46:03.266 --> 00:46:04.801
I prepared a mini feast

722
00:46:04.934 --> 00:46:08.004
to honor our beautiful friend.

723
00:46:08.138 --> 00:46:11.941
I got Pecorino Nero,
Parmigiano-Reggiano, Manchego,

724
00:46:12.075 --> 00:46:14.612
- and, of course...
- Thanks.

725
00:46:14.745 --> 00:46:16.112
- He loved Brie.
- Yeah.

726
00:46:16.246 --> 00:46:19.583
- Ah! And wine.
- Especially wine.

727
00:46:19.717 --> 00:46:21.652
Wow, I thought
you guys were gonna serve,

728
00:46:21.786 --> 00:46:23.453
like, bean sprouts
and wheatgrass.

729
00:46:23.587 --> 00:46:25.723
Eating is all
about the intention

730
00:46:25.855 --> 00:46:26.990
you put into your meal.

731
00:46:27.123 --> 00:46:28.358
If you honor the cow,

732
00:46:28.491 --> 00:46:30.860
the cheese is
gonna be good for you.

733
00:46:30.994 --> 00:46:32.962
By the way, I understand
the circumstances

734
00:46:33.096 --> 00:46:35.031
that brought you here
have been stressful.

735
00:46:35.165 --> 00:46:37.802
- So stressful.
- If you ever need to talk,

736
00:46:37.934 --> 00:46:39.336
I'm a licensed
psychotherapist.

737
00:46:39.469 --> 00:46:42.238
Wow. I can really see
why you guys call him...

738
00:46:42.372 --> 00:46:45.175
- The Saint.
- Yes. Okay.

739
00:46:45.308 --> 00:46:48.211
- Oh, electrolyte-enhanced water?
- Mm, fine.

740
00:46:48.345 --> 00:46:51.348
Oh, and also try this. It's
really good for your breath.

741
00:46:52.717 --> 00:46:54.951
- Oh, thank you.
- Good.

742
00:46:58.254 --> 00:47:00.825
I sent the ID of the last person
to access the vault

743
00:47:00.957 --> 00:47:03.193
through our search system,
ran every CCTV

744
00:47:03.326 --> 00:47:06.196
and security cam
in Hamburg.

745
00:47:06.329 --> 00:47:09.299
Fleming. That's my... That's
the guy that buried my report.

746
00:47:09.432 --> 00:47:11.702
- Hm.
- Look. There.

747
00:47:11.836 --> 00:47:14.137
He was at the airport
five hours ago.

748
00:47:14.270 --> 00:47:16.206
- So he's left Germany.
- With the case.

749
00:47:16.339 --> 00:47:18.174
He knows exactly
what Calisto can do.

750
00:47:18.308 --> 00:47:20.377
He knows what it's worth
on the black market.

751
00:47:20.511 --> 00:47:22.813
If he's selling it,
he'd want you out of the way.

752
00:47:22.946 --> 00:47:24.615
- I'm broadening the search.
- I'm sorry.

753
00:47:24.749 --> 00:47:26.216
Fleming tried
to have me killed?

754
00:47:26.349 --> 00:47:29.219
Maybe. Maybe at
the direction of a buyer.

755
00:47:29.352 --> 00:47:32.122
Bad guys don't like loose ends,
you made a fancy new toy...

756
00:47:32.255 --> 00:47:34.525
But I worked for him.
I mean...

757
00:47:36.426 --> 00:47:37.595
he flirted with me.

758
00:47:37.728 --> 00:47:39.195
Oh, honey.

759
00:47:39.329 --> 00:47:41.264
A man can love you
and want you dead.

760
00:47:41.398 --> 00:47:43.199
Ha, not me.

761
00:47:43.333 --> 00:47:45.034
There was a gunfight
at my wedding.

762
00:47:45.168 --> 00:47:48.271
- Wait, you're married?
- No. I was the better shot.

763
00:47:49.673 --> 00:47:50.974
All right. I need cheese.

764
00:47:51.107 --> 00:47:52.976
"Cheese." Is that
a code for something?

765
00:47:53.109 --> 00:47:55.780
Yes. It's code for
"I'm 40 and single,

766
00:47:55.912 --> 00:47:58.849
and I have a cheese-size hole
in my soul to fill."

767
00:47:58.982 --> 00:48:01.050
I also have vegan ice cream
for your soul.

768
00:48:01.184 --> 00:48:02.686
You really know what I need.

769
00:48:02.820 --> 00:48:04.555
I should have
just gone around Fleming

770
00:48:04.688 --> 00:48:07.090
and not followed
some stupid chain of command.

771
00:48:07.223 --> 00:48:11.094
Gone directly to Brok.
But, no, I just rolled over.

772
00:48:11.227 --> 00:48:12.696
You're probably
the last people

773
00:48:12.830 --> 00:48:14.532
that would know
what that feels like.

774
00:48:14.665 --> 00:48:17.066
I grew up with
major abandonment issues.

775
00:48:17.200 --> 00:48:19.402
It led to some pretty
self-sabotaging behavior,

776
00:48:19.537 --> 00:48:22.740
which landed me in various
institutional facilities.

777
00:48:22.873 --> 00:48:24.441
Charlie bailed me out.

778
00:48:24.575 --> 00:48:26.376
And if it wasn't
for Charlie...

779
00:48:28.211 --> 00:48:31.481
I'd probably be dead or back
in prison, so I feel you.

780
00:48:31.615 --> 00:48:35.251
I pretty much grew up on the
corner of powerless and ashamed.

781
00:48:35.385 --> 00:48:38.154
Wait. You grew up on Park
Avenue. Aren't you an heiress?

782
00:48:39.790 --> 00:48:41.692
More money, more problems.

783
00:48:41.826 --> 00:48:44.461
So, what about you?
How did Charlie find you?

784
00:48:44.595 --> 00:48:47.631
Jane is former MI6.
Youngest recruit ever.

785
00:48:47.765 --> 00:48:49.432
You worked
for British intelligence?

786
00:48:49.567 --> 00:48:51.502
She said "former."

787
00:48:51.635 --> 00:48:53.369
I also followed the rules.

788
00:48:53.504 --> 00:48:57.006
The chain of command didn't
work out so well for me either.

789
00:48:59.275 --> 00:49:01.010
Ralph's dead.

790
00:49:01.144 --> 00:49:02.947
I killed Ralph.

791
00:49:03.079 --> 00:49:04.247
I'm... I'm a murderer.

792
00:49:04.380 --> 00:49:05.583
- No.
- No, no, no.

793
00:49:05.716 --> 00:49:07.116
Collateral damage.

794
00:49:07.250 --> 00:49:08.819
I wouldn't take that on.

795
00:49:08.953 --> 00:49:12.455
The point is, if Calisto
falls in the wrong hands...

796
00:49:12.590 --> 00:49:16.125
I mean, we have to get it back
before it hurts more people.

797
00:49:18.328 --> 00:49:20.296
Well, now's our chance.

798
00:49:20.430 --> 00:49:23.299
Mr. Fleming just cleared
passport control in Istanbul.

799
00:49:24.467 --> 00:49:26.804
- Oh, no.
- No.

800
00:49:26.937 --> 00:49:28.772
What's your problem
with Istanbul?

801
00:49:28.906 --> 00:49:30.841
I got food poisoning
from undercooked lamb

802
00:49:30.975 --> 00:49:33.376
and yogurt sauce I left out,
but then I got hungry.

803
00:49:33.511 --> 00:49:36.412
- What about you?
- Not that.

804
00:49:36.547 --> 00:49:37.715
Will you excuse us?

805
00:49:40.149 --> 00:49:41.585
We'll be right back.

806
00:49:44.153 --> 00:49:48.091
I wanna be sure that assassin
stays away from us.

807
00:49:48.224 --> 00:49:51.227
We should keep this quiet until
we know who all the players are.

808
00:49:51.361 --> 00:49:53.731
We don't know what this
Calisto is or who wants it,

809
00:49:53.864 --> 00:49:56.199
so let's play it safe.

810
00:49:56.332 --> 00:49:59.168
What about
Ralph-killer in there?

811
00:49:59.302 --> 00:50:01.572
Take her to the closet,
gear her up.

812
00:50:01.705 --> 00:50:05.543
And if anybody asks,
we're going to Brazil.

813
00:50:05.676 --> 00:50:07.578
Okay.

814
00:50:23.694 --> 00:50:24.695
Istanbul.

815
00:50:29.299 --> 00:50:30.668
What about Elena Houghlin?

816
00:50:30.801 --> 00:50:32.870
I think you know what to do.

817
00:50:50.386 --> 00:50:51.655
<i>I took it apart.</i>

818
00:50:51.789 --> 00:50:55.091
Nothing. No tracker.

819
00:50:56.292 --> 00:50:58.394
It's not emitting
any signals.

820
00:50:58.529 --> 00:50:59.597
What had you worried?

821
00:51:01.230 --> 00:51:02.900
To be honest, I don't know.

822
00:51:03.033 --> 00:51:04.400
A feeling.

823
00:51:04.535 --> 00:51:06.369
Something in the bones.
Hmph.

824
00:51:06.503 --> 00:51:08.271
Old habits.

825
00:51:08.404 --> 00:51:10.908
Perhaps it's simply
that you miss the job.

826
00:51:11.041 --> 00:51:12.977
We all get old, my friend.

827
00:51:13.109 --> 00:51:15.445
Retirement is not
a death sentence.

828
00:51:15.579 --> 00:51:18.314
Says the man
who refuses to retire.

829
00:51:20.951 --> 00:51:22.418
Mm, come on.

830
00:51:30.527 --> 00:51:32.763
What?

831
00:51:38.267 --> 00:51:40.303
Something in the bones,
indeed.

832
00:51:40.436 --> 00:51:42.039
Who would do this to you?

833
00:51:49.445 --> 00:51:52.348
Someone who knows
I'm on to her.

834
00:51:54.818 --> 00:51:56.020
Thank you.

835
00:52:11.401 --> 00:52:13.637
Look at this.

836
00:52:14.972 --> 00:52:18.108
This is the closet
of my dreams.

837
00:52:18.241 --> 00:52:20.644
And I just get
to take whatever I want?

838
00:52:20.778 --> 00:52:23.147
- Borrow.
- Oh.

839
00:52:23.279 --> 00:52:25.015
Is that an actual rule?

840
00:52:25.149 --> 00:52:29.820
Okay. So you wanna start
with a protective base layer.

841
00:52:29.953 --> 00:52:33.524
I recommend
a beaded camisole. Yeah?

842
00:52:33.657 --> 00:52:36.225
Oh. Some kind
of polymer material.

843
00:52:36.359 --> 00:52:38.929
Uh, bulletproof,
composite body armor.

844
00:52:39.063 --> 00:52:42.231
It was originally developed as a
protective layer for spacecraft.

845
00:52:42.365 --> 00:52:45.769
Yeah. And it's a bra
that doesn't dig. Progress.

846
00:52:45.903 --> 00:52:48.404
How we doing down here?

847
00:52:48.539 --> 00:52:50.373
Ah, we're still
in the first closet.

848
00:52:52.810 --> 00:52:54.277
There's another closet?

849
00:52:54.410 --> 00:52:56.345
Hm. Armory open.

850
00:53:00.216 --> 00:53:01.719
Jane, I wanna show
you something.

851
00:53:06.389 --> 00:53:09.258
- Whoa.
- Come on, check it out.

852
00:53:10.661 --> 00:53:12.361
- Here, try these on.
- Oh, thank you.

853
00:53:12.495 --> 00:53:14.598
Why? What do they do? Whoa!

854
00:53:14.732 --> 00:53:17.000
What do they do? Whoa.

855
00:53:19.503 --> 00:53:21.772
Huh. You're younger
than I thought.

856
00:53:21.905 --> 00:53:23.107
I've lived hard.

857
00:53:23.239 --> 00:53:25.109
Think you can put
that MIT degree to use

858
00:53:25.241 --> 00:53:27.010
- with something like this?
- What is it?

859
00:53:27.144 --> 00:53:29.747
Universal Interface. Lets you
hack into almost anything.

860
00:53:29.880 --> 00:53:32.850
Mm-mm, not almost anything.
Everything.

861
00:53:32.983 --> 00:53:35.284
- So here's the new baby.
- What's that?

862
00:53:35.418 --> 00:53:40.256
High-velocity rifle, customized
to fire tranquilizer darts.

863
00:53:40.389 --> 00:53:42.659
The load: nonlethal,
fast-acting, very potent.

864
00:53:42.793 --> 00:53:44.393
Jane, you have
a new cuddle buddy.

865
00:53:45.629 --> 00:53:46.897
Oh, Jesus.

866
00:53:47.030 --> 00:53:48.832
Shall we fit Elena
with comms?

867
00:53:48.966 --> 00:53:50.234
I think so.

868
00:53:50.366 --> 00:53:52.301
Oh, that in-ear radio thing
you guys have?

869
00:53:52.435 --> 00:53:53.804
Ah, even better.

870
00:53:53.937 --> 00:53:55.572
It's a subdermal transmitter.

871
00:53:55.706 --> 00:53:57.908
Works through
bone conduction. See?

872
00:53:58.041 --> 00:53:59.643
So I'm getting a tattoo?

873
00:54:01.310 --> 00:54:03.981
Uh, no. Tattoos are earned
by Angels over time.

874
00:54:04.114 --> 00:54:05.749
You'll get
a less permanent version.

875
00:54:05.883 --> 00:54:08.952
Yeah, comms are concealed
in the link.

876
00:54:09.086 --> 00:54:11.121
As long as you have it on,
you can hear us.

877
00:54:11.255 --> 00:54:14.124
Cool. Hey, can I take
these mints?

878
00:54:14.258 --> 00:54:16.425
No. Avoid the mints.

879
00:54:16.560 --> 00:54:18.996
Actually, let's just stop
the touching around here.

880
00:54:19.129 --> 00:54:21.430
- You know, some of this blows up.
- Oh.

881
00:54:36.479 --> 00:54:38.182
This place is amazing.

882
00:54:38.314 --> 00:54:41.051
It's the crossroads of the world.
Danger and money.

883
00:54:41.185 --> 00:54:44.188
We need to figure out where
Mr. Fleming's meeting his buyer

884
00:54:44.320 --> 00:54:46.056
and get Calisto back
before it becomes

885
00:54:46.190 --> 00:54:48.457
every bad guy's
favorite new weapon.

886
00:54:48.592 --> 00:54:51.494
- Like suitcase nukes.
- Pet tigers.

887
00:54:51.628 --> 00:54:53.697
- Jet Skis.
- Sea-Doos.

888
00:54:53.831 --> 00:54:56.533
Cars that go fast
really furiously.

889
00:54:56.667 --> 00:54:57.968
So how do we find him?

890
00:54:58.101 --> 00:55:01.171
Well, we're off
the agency's grid here, so...

891
00:55:01.305 --> 00:55:05.642
How do we find him? We hit
the streets. We go old-school.

892
00:55:05.776 --> 00:55:08.411
We sling some bills.
We get violent.

893
00:55:08.545 --> 00:55:10.547
I feel like a tiger today,
maybe a leopard.

894
00:55:10.681 --> 00:55:12.950
But either way,
I am down to get wild.

895
00:55:13.083 --> 00:55:14.350
I might have
a contact here.

896
00:55:14.483 --> 00:55:16.153
An asset
from when I was with MI6.

897
00:55:16.286 --> 00:55:17.521
Uh, "might" as in?

898
00:55:17.654 --> 00:55:19.156
As in she definitely
lives here,

899
00:55:19.289 --> 00:55:20.991
and she definitely hates me.

900
00:55:31.602 --> 00:55:33.170
Practice your English?

901
00:55:33.303 --> 00:55:35.172
- Good morning.
- Good morning. Well done.

902
00:55:35.305 --> 00:55:37.574
- Candy!
- Candy.

903
00:55:39.776 --> 00:55:41.645
Still spoiling
the local kids?

904
00:55:42.980 --> 00:55:45.549
You. Get away from me.

905
00:55:45.682 --> 00:55:48.919
Fatima, wait.
Please, just talk to me.

906
00:55:49.052 --> 00:55:51.788
Talk to someone else. I can't
get involved with you again.

907
00:55:51.922 --> 00:55:53.223
Fatima, please wait.

908
00:55:53.357 --> 00:55:55.424
I waited for you already.

909
00:55:55.559 --> 00:55:57.393
Remember?

910
00:55:57.527 --> 00:56:01.131
And I wasn't there for you, but
I don't work for MI6 anymore.

911
00:56:01.265 --> 00:56:03.867
- I work for these people now.
- I don't care.

912
00:56:04.001 --> 00:56:05.434
I don't help you.

913
00:56:05.569 --> 00:56:07.771
You know why.

914
00:56:07.905 --> 00:56:11.108
They are very well-funded.
Non-governmental, NGO.

915
00:56:11.241 --> 00:56:14.278
They can get whatever you need
to get up and running today.

916
00:56:14.410 --> 00:56:17.080
No waiting.
No broken promises.

917
00:56:24.321 --> 00:56:25.589
Thank you.

918
00:56:25.722 --> 00:56:27.624
It's only tea.

919
00:56:29.393 --> 00:56:31.228
What do you want from me?

920
00:56:39.269 --> 00:56:41.071
Have you seen this man?

921
00:56:44.341 --> 00:56:45.642
Maybe...

922
00:56:46.710 --> 00:56:48.477
you know someone who has.

923
00:56:50.647 --> 00:56:52.983
Please. I can help you.

924
00:56:53.116 --> 00:56:54.851
Rebuild the clinic.

925
00:56:54.985 --> 00:56:58.155
- You can help me now?
- I'm sorry.

926
00:56:58.288 --> 00:57:01.158
I believed them when they
told me my asset was safe.

927
00:57:01.291 --> 00:57:03.860
And I believed you,
but I lost everything.

928
00:57:03.994 --> 00:57:08.031
I had to turn away unwed mothers
I could no longer help.

929
00:57:08.165 --> 00:57:09.465
I know.

930
00:57:11.568 --> 00:57:13.770
It's why I quit.

931
00:57:16.506 --> 00:57:18.909
But let me rebuild our trust.

932
00:57:22.079 --> 00:57:23.513
I brought you the usual.

933
00:57:26.550 --> 00:57:28.118
It's right outside.

934
00:57:33.924 --> 00:57:35.025
Show me.

935
00:57:38.261 --> 00:57:40.764
I can get you another shipment
in six months.

936
00:57:40.897 --> 00:57:41.999
Four.

937
00:57:45.802 --> 00:57:48.839
So how long will it take
for your sources to find our guy?

938
00:57:48.972 --> 00:57:50.574
Because we really need to...

939
00:57:54.111 --> 00:57:56.146
Is this what
the doctor ordered?

940
00:57:56.279 --> 00:57:59.182
Okay. Let's get this
off the street.

941
00:57:59.316 --> 00:58:00.317
All right.

942
00:58:03.620 --> 00:58:04.654
Good job, Jane.

943
00:58:10.227 --> 00:58:14.064
Your man is in a hotel.
The Pasha Hotel.

944
00:58:14.197 --> 00:58:16.366
The Ibrahim Pasha?

945
00:58:16.501 --> 00:58:19.002
Do you know anybody
who can get us into his room?

946
00:58:19.136 --> 00:58:20.337
Of course.

947
00:58:20.470 --> 00:58:22.507
I will take the van too.

948
00:58:30.047 --> 00:58:31.548
Of course.

949
00:58:35.352 --> 00:58:37.020
Pasha. Let's go.

950
00:58:49.199 --> 00:58:53.236
<i>Let's learn all we can about
Mr. Fleming's trip to Istanbul.</i>

951
00:58:53.370 --> 00:58:56.740
<i>When Fleming goes out,
we go in.</i>

952
00:58:59.743 --> 00:59:02.646
<i>Double his devices.
Gather all his communications.</i>

953
00:59:02.779 --> 00:59:06.049
<i>The when, the where, the who.</i>

954
00:59:06.183 --> 00:59:09.386
He's been looking at property
in Costa Rica.

955
00:59:09.520 --> 00:59:12.722
And he's got
an offshore bank account.

956
00:59:12.856 --> 00:59:14.825
Gotcha.

957
00:59:22.599 --> 00:59:24.701
<i>What about me?
What should I do?</i>

958
00:59:24.835 --> 00:59:27.904
<i>Seeing as you're supposed to be
dead, why don't you relax.</i>

959
00:59:28.038 --> 00:59:30.407
<i>Fleming could recognize you,
and we can't risk it.</i>

960
00:59:34.878 --> 00:59:36.880
No, thank you. Full.

961
00:59:51.228 --> 00:59:52.829
<i>Let's get in there.</i>

962
01:00:05.510 --> 01:00:07.677
<i>Jane, he's almost there.</i>

963
01:00:07.811 --> 01:00:09.646
<i>Sabina, text him now.</i>

964
01:00:22.759 --> 01:00:24.361
Sir, is everything all right?

965
01:00:24.494 --> 01:00:25.996
No, I can't find my hat.

966
01:00:26.129 --> 01:00:27.598
Let me help you with that.

967
01:00:27.731 --> 01:00:29.534
- Your hat.
- Thank you. Yes. Thank you.

968
01:00:29.666 --> 01:00:31.468
Have you seen my phone?

969
01:00:33.670 --> 01:00:35.172
- Your bag.
- Oh, thanks.

970
01:00:36.574 --> 01:00:38.341
- Oh, there it is.
- Thank you.

971
01:00:42.445 --> 01:00:45.148
<i>Alrighty, here it is.
We filtered his communications,</i>

972
01:00:45.282 --> 01:00:47.552
and it seems Mr. Fleming
is selling Calisto

973
01:00:47.684 --> 01:00:49.620
tomorrow
at the Turkish derby.

974
01:00:49.753 --> 01:00:52.055
Veliefendi Hippodrome.

975
01:00:52.189 --> 01:00:53.823
<i>Of course,
this particular racetrack</i>

976
01:00:53.957 --> 01:00:56.359
<i>is popular with a syndicate
of wealthy businessmen.</i>

977
01:00:56.493 --> 01:00:57.928
<i>No doubt with connections</i>

978
01:00:58.061 --> 01:00:59.930
<i>to international arms deals,
drug trade and...</i>

979
01:01:00.063 --> 01:01:02.432
<i>All parties who might
be interested in Calisto.</i>

980
01:01:02.567 --> 01:01:04.234
<i>Familiarize yourselves:
syndicate members,</i>

981
01:01:04.367 --> 01:01:05.936
<i>wealthy horse owners
expected to attend.</i>

982
01:01:06.069 --> 01:01:08.205
<i>Flag anyone Fleming
could be in business with.</i>

983
01:01:08.338 --> 01:01:09.540
I wanna help.

984
01:01:11.141 --> 01:01:13.710
Look, I am not
just some frightened girl

985
01:01:13.843 --> 01:01:15.946
in your witness
protection program.

986
01:01:16.079 --> 01:01:19.182
If you need help getting in and
out of someplace, I can do it.

987
01:01:19.316 --> 01:01:22.719
I can hack any system,
and I can do it fast.

988
01:01:22.852 --> 01:01:24.622
You need me, Mrs. Bosley.

989
01:01:24.754 --> 01:01:27.658
And don't tell me I can't do it
because I know I can.

990
01:01:27.791 --> 01:01:29.993
I am... I'm done
sitting still. I'm...

991
01:01:30.126 --> 01:01:32.829
I've had a taste.
I want more.

992
01:01:34.464 --> 01:01:35.566
I want in.

993
01:01:37.400 --> 01:01:40.504
You know, I once saw
a really fat baby

994
01:01:40.638 --> 01:01:43.440
giving Eskimo kisses
to a kitten.

995
01:01:44.841 --> 01:01:47.410
And that was more adorable.

996
01:01:47.545 --> 01:01:49.446
Also, it's implied
that you're coming

997
01:01:49.580 --> 01:01:51.214
because you're in
this briefing.

998
01:01:51.348 --> 01:01:53.584
Yeah, she gave you
the universal hacking tool

999
01:01:53.718 --> 01:01:56.019
and the bracelet,
right?

1000
01:01:56.152 --> 01:01:57.921
Mm-hm. Yeah.

1001
01:01:58.054 --> 01:02:02.259
But how'd that feel? It looked
like it felt really good.

1002
01:02:02.392 --> 01:02:04.494
- Felt nice.
- I was just gonna give you

1003
01:02:04.629 --> 01:02:07.632
- the tablet once I was done.
- Mm.

1004
01:02:10.967 --> 01:02:13.136
- Uh, carry on.
- Great.

1005
01:02:13.270 --> 01:02:15.105
As I was about to say,

1006
01:02:15.238 --> 01:02:16.741
<i>there's a lot of ground
to cover,</i>

1007
01:02:16.873 --> 01:02:18.775
<i>so we're gonna need
to spread out.</i>

1008
01:02:18.908 --> 01:02:21.512
<i>Elena, you'll be
our eye in the sky.</i>

1009
01:02:21.646 --> 01:02:25.348
<i>The track's mainframe's located
just inside the press box.</i>

1010
01:02:25.482 --> 01:02:28.586
<i>We'll get you in. You hack
into the security cameras.</i>

1011
01:02:28.719 --> 01:02:30.153
<i>Watch for Mr. Fleming.</i>

1012
01:02:34.257 --> 01:02:35.825
<i>Jane's on crowd control.</i>

1013
01:02:35.959 --> 01:02:38.228
<i>Turkish derby attracts
thousands of spectators</i>

1014
01:02:38.361 --> 01:02:40.631
<i>who need to be scanned
and assessed.</i>

1015
01:02:44.067 --> 01:02:45.435
<i>Start low, go high.</i>

1016
01:02:45.569 --> 01:02:46.803
<i>From your nest,</i>

1017
01:02:46.936 --> 01:02:48.438
<i>you can provide
tactical support.</i>

1018
01:02:48.572 --> 01:02:52.075
<i>Take out any threats
to the operation.</i>

1019
01:02:52.208 --> 01:02:54.512
<i>Sabina, you'll run
the ground game.</i>

1020
01:02:54.645 --> 01:02:56.846
<i>Once the target's on site,
you make the grab.</i>

1021
01:02:56.980 --> 01:02:59.784
<i>We need Fleming,
his buyer and Calisto.</i>

1022
01:02:59.916 --> 01:03:01.184
<i>No loose ends.</i>

1023
01:03:04.354 --> 01:03:06.022
<i>I'll take care
of the transportation</i>

1024
01:03:06.156 --> 01:03:07.725
<i>and prep for extraction.</i>

1025
01:03:07.857 --> 01:03:09.893
<i>We're taking everybody
out of there with us.</i>

1026
01:03:10.026 --> 01:03:12.395
<i>I have just the vehicle
to do it.</i>

1027
01:03:12.530 --> 01:03:15.666
Okay, and I'm in.

1028
01:03:19.670 --> 01:03:21.004
Hey, Jane.

1029
01:03:21.137 --> 01:03:23.373
Ah, there you are.

1030
01:03:27.511 --> 01:03:28.878
Comm check. Sabina.

1031
01:03:29.012 --> 01:03:29.979
Good.

1032
01:03:30.113 --> 01:03:31.515
- <i>Jane.</i>
- Good.

1033
01:03:31.649 --> 01:03:34.117
- Elena.
- <i>Good.</i>

1034
01:03:34.250 --> 01:03:35.653
Don't talk into your bracelet.

1035
01:03:37.755 --> 01:03:39.989
I just missed a superfecta.

1036
01:03:40.123 --> 01:03:42.793
Better luck in the third run,
I hope.

1037
01:03:44.528 --> 01:03:46.196
Hey, what's your bet?

1038
01:03:47.698 --> 01:03:48.965
Um...

1039
01:03:51.434 --> 01:03:52.837
The blue one.

1040
01:03:53.870 --> 01:03:55.138
Mm.

1041
01:03:58.375 --> 01:04:00.910
Six minutes to post time.
Anybody see anything?

1042
01:04:02.379 --> 01:04:03.614
Nothing yet.

1043
01:04:07.852 --> 01:04:09.886
<i>Jane, you got anything yet?</i>

1044
01:04:10.019 --> 01:04:11.221
Nothing.

1045
01:04:19.329 --> 01:04:22.031
Excuse me, who is that?

1046
01:04:22.165 --> 01:04:23.701
Alim Hassan.

1047
01:04:23.834 --> 01:04:24.934
Qatari prince.

1048
01:04:25.068 --> 01:04:27.638
- Oh, "Qatari prince."
- Yeah, serious money.

1049
01:04:27.772 --> 01:04:29.874
- "Serious money."
- Owns hundreds of horses.

1050
01:04:30.006 --> 01:04:32.375
- "Owns hundreds of horses"?
- Yeah.

1051
01:04:33.811 --> 01:04:34.911
<i>We get it. He's rich.</i>

1052
01:04:35.044 --> 01:04:36.614
Is he the buyer?

1053
01:04:36.747 --> 01:04:38.516
<i>I don't have an angle.</i>

1054
01:04:38.649 --> 01:04:41.217
Sabina! Fleming.

1055
01:04:41.351 --> 01:04:43.920
<i>That's him. Light blue suit!</i>

1056
01:04:49.225 --> 01:04:50.761
Yeah, he's here.

1057
01:04:50.895 --> 01:04:53.363
That's definitely him. Sabina?

1058
01:04:53.496 --> 01:04:54.632
Got him.

1059
01:04:56.667 --> 01:04:57.768
He has the goods.

1060
01:04:57.902 --> 01:04:59.537
Moving in.

1061
01:05:02.238 --> 01:05:03.139
Jane?

1062
01:05:06.911 --> 01:05:08.813
In my sights. Boz?

1063
01:05:08.945 --> 01:05:10.146
The ride is ready.

1064
01:05:14.718 --> 01:05:16.787
He's talking to somebody.
Gray suit.

1065
01:05:16.921 --> 01:05:18.288
Is that the buyer?

1066
01:05:22.158 --> 01:05:25.295
- It's the assassin.
- Bae showed up.

1067
01:05:25.428 --> 01:05:27.130
If you think you're
killing him before I kill him

1068
01:05:27.263 --> 01:05:28.131
I'll kill you first.

1069
01:05:28.264 --> 01:05:29.867
Take the shot, Jane. Bag him.

1070
01:05:33.470 --> 01:05:34.971
In the car? All right.

1071
01:05:40.544 --> 01:05:42.145
- Oh, shit.
- They're in the Mercedes.

1072
01:05:42.278 --> 01:05:44.849
- There's no sale here.
- We gotta go! Get down here.

1073
01:05:44.981 --> 01:05:46.149
I'm coming!

1074
01:05:47.083 --> 01:05:48.786
Shit, shit!

1075
01:05:48.919 --> 01:05:50.186
Shit!

1076
01:05:52.790 --> 01:05:54.758
<i>Get a tracker on that Mercedes!</i>

1077
01:05:54.892 --> 01:05:56.125
On it!

1078
01:06:09.105 --> 01:06:10.406
Come on! Hyah!

1079
01:06:16.379 --> 01:06:18.214
Come on.

1080
01:06:18.348 --> 01:06:19.517
Coming in!

1081
01:06:22.118 --> 01:06:23.587
Come on. Move, move, move.

1082
01:06:23.721 --> 01:06:25.689
- <i>Come on, Elena!</i>
- I'm coming!

1083
01:06:37.868 --> 01:06:39.168
Go, go, go!

1084
01:06:41.605 --> 01:06:42.840
Come on!

1085
01:07:10.366 --> 01:07:11.635
- Giddyup.
- Sabina!

1086
01:07:11.769 --> 01:07:13.102
- Hey, guys.
- Get in here.

1087
01:07:15.071 --> 01:07:16.439
Okay, punch it.

1088
01:07:16.574 --> 01:07:18.408
- Here we go! Great job!
- Whoo!

1089
01:07:18.542 --> 01:07:22.478
How did you...? I didn't know
you could jump horses.

1090
01:07:22.613 --> 01:07:25.481
- More money, more horses.
- Huh.

1091
01:07:25.616 --> 01:07:27.918
Can somebody
please track this mofo?

1092
01:07:29.053 --> 01:07:30.621
We cannot tail him in this.

1093
01:07:32.422 --> 01:07:33.724
Hold on.

1094
01:07:45.869 --> 01:07:47.571
They're headed north
out of town.

1095
01:07:52.710 --> 01:07:54.310
We've left city limits.

1096
01:07:54.444 --> 01:07:56.947
There's nothing out here
but a rock quarry.

1097
01:07:59.349 --> 01:08:00.416
Bring up the specs.

1098
01:08:20.303 --> 01:08:22.806
I'll circle until you signal.

1099
01:08:22.940 --> 01:08:25.208
The sale will definitely
go down here.

1100
01:08:25.341 --> 01:08:27.811
Let's take everything.
We don't know who's in there.

1101
01:08:27.945 --> 01:08:30.146
I-I think
I'm a little overdressed.

1102
01:08:32.950 --> 01:08:35.119
Okay, um...

1103
01:08:35.251 --> 01:08:36.687
You need this.

1104
01:08:52.168 --> 01:08:53.504
I see a way in.

1105
01:08:53.637 --> 01:08:56.140
Ja... Jane! Jane!

1106
01:09:01.912 --> 01:09:03.047
Come on.

1107
01:09:24.134 --> 01:09:25.268
Huh?

1108
01:09:29.740 --> 01:09:30.874
In your dreams.

1109
01:09:35.478 --> 01:09:37.614
Hi.

1110
01:09:42.019 --> 01:09:44.722
Hey, he's gonna wake up.
Come on.

1111
01:09:50.194 --> 01:09:51.662
You've got all the dots.

1112
01:09:51.795 --> 01:09:53.564
I signaled you,
you went rogue.

1113
01:09:53.697 --> 01:09:55.833
- Should we toss him?
- Yeah, let's do it.

1114
01:10:01.705 --> 01:10:04.340
Man. Whoever Fleming's
in business with,

1115
01:10:04.474 --> 01:10:06.375
he is in
way over his head.

1116
01:10:06.510 --> 01:10:09.378
Seal that gate.
Lock them in.

1117
01:10:09.513 --> 01:10:11.849
- Then lock yourself in here.
- Okay.

1118
01:10:12.983 --> 01:10:14.017
These are for you.

1119
01:10:15.652 --> 01:10:17.121
They are not mints.

1120
01:10:17.253 --> 01:10:19.623
- You got it?
- Not mints.

1121
01:10:19.757 --> 01:10:21.457
- Let's go.
- Lock this. Not mints.

1122
01:10:21.592 --> 01:10:22.960
- No, I know.
- Lock it!

1123
01:10:38.208 --> 01:10:41.145
Okay, the gate is locked. Only
other exit is up three stories.

1124
01:10:41.277 --> 01:10:42.613
Nicely done, Elena.

1125
01:11:02.766 --> 01:11:04.467
There he is.

1126
01:11:04.601 --> 01:11:06.970
- Mr. Fleming.
- Yes.

1127
01:11:07.104 --> 01:11:08.605
That's Australian Jonny.

1128
01:11:08.739 --> 01:11:10.607
Didn't we hand him
over to the Americans?

1129
01:11:10.741 --> 01:11:11.742
Well, he's here.

1130
01:11:11.875 --> 01:11:13.510
If you think
you're gonna kill me

1131
01:11:13.644 --> 01:11:14.945
before I kill him...

1132
01:11:16.312 --> 01:11:17.614
What was the thing
you said?

1133
01:11:17.748 --> 01:11:20.684
So, uh, you are...?

1134
01:11:20.818 --> 01:11:23.452
I represent a buyer
who wishes to remain anonymous.

1135
01:11:23.587 --> 01:11:24.888
Ah.

1136
01:11:25.022 --> 01:11:27.558
- Let's have a look.
- Of course.

1137
01:11:29.293 --> 01:11:30.694
<i>Guys, that's Calisto.</i>

1138
01:11:30.828 --> 01:11:32.663
There we go.

1139
01:11:35.098 --> 01:11:36.900
The money?

1140
01:11:37.034 --> 01:11:37.968
COD.

1141
01:11:39.435 --> 01:11:41.038
Plus wire transfer.

1142
01:11:43.273 --> 01:11:44.340
Great.

1143
01:11:44.473 --> 01:11:46.210
But before we close the deal,

1144
01:11:46.342 --> 01:11:48.512
my employer would like
a little demonstration

1145
01:11:48.645 --> 01:11:53.016
just to make sure
the devices do what you say.

1146
01:11:57.353 --> 01:11:59.690
You want me
to kill somebody?

1147
01:11:59.823 --> 01:12:01.191
Damn.

1148
01:12:01.325 --> 01:12:04.360
No, I don't,
but my employer insists.

1149
01:12:04.493 --> 01:12:07.197
<i>So, yes. Pick anybody.</i>

1150
01:12:07.331 --> 01:12:09.967
- Obviously, don't pick me.
- Uh...

1151
01:12:11.367 --> 01:12:14.671
- Sidam, go get somebody.
- Uh, no, no, no.

1152
01:12:14.805 --> 01:12:18.474
Uh, I-I-I gave you
the report.

1153
01:12:18.609 --> 01:12:23.080
It's all outlined in there, so
that was never part of the deal.

1154
01:12:23.213 --> 01:12:26.415
<i>Well, Mr. Fleming,
it is now.</i>

1155
01:12:26.550 --> 01:12:30.187
<i>Look, it's a complicated process.
Obviously, I don't...</i>

1156
01:12:30.320 --> 01:12:32.189
You don't even know
how it works, do you?

1157
01:12:32.322 --> 01:12:33.924
<i>It'll require root access</i>

1158
01:12:34.057 --> 01:12:35.792
or a world-class hacker.

1159
01:12:37.127 --> 01:12:39.363
Whoa, whoa!

1160
01:12:39.495 --> 01:12:41.531
What are you thinking?
Bloody hell!

1161
01:12:41.665 --> 01:12:44.201
That was not part of the plan,
Mr. Hodak!

1162
01:12:45.269 --> 01:12:46.236
Damn it!

1163
01:12:47.504 --> 01:12:48.739
Boz, Fleming is down.

1164
01:12:48.872 --> 01:12:52.242
<i>The assassin works
for Jonny Smith.</i>

1165
01:12:52.376 --> 01:12:53.911
<i>Boz.</i>

1166
01:12:54.044 --> 01:12:55.746
We need to engage.
Ready for exfil?

1167
01:12:55.879 --> 01:12:58.782
Let's get out of here! Someone
grab that. Get me out of here.

1168
01:13:00.851 --> 01:13:02.686
Boz, they are leaving.

1169
01:13:02.819 --> 01:13:03.954
<i>Go, no-go?</i>

1170
01:13:05.355 --> 01:13:07.224
Where the hell is she?

1171
01:13:07.357 --> 01:13:08.792
I can't see her anywhere.

1172
01:13:12.562 --> 01:13:13.530
It won't open.

1173
01:13:13.664 --> 01:13:15.065
Well, then fix it.

1174
01:13:15.198 --> 01:13:16.934
Go upstairs and fix it.

1175
01:13:21.371 --> 01:13:23.140
Oh, no.
Guys, someone's coming.

1176
01:13:24.440 --> 01:13:25.809
<i>He's headed your way.</i>

1177
01:13:46.563 --> 01:13:47.463
Together.

1178
01:14:03.246 --> 01:14:04.781
- Up there!
- Shit.

1179
01:14:06.416 --> 01:14:08.285
- Find them!
- Oh, my God. Guys?

1180
01:14:08.418 --> 01:14:09.686
- Go!
- <i>What's happening?</i>

1181
01:14:11.288 --> 01:14:13.489
I'll take the assassin.
Cover me.

1182
01:14:13.623 --> 01:14:15.692
Go. Go, go, go!

1183
01:14:29.272 --> 01:14:32.009
Oh, Miss Independent.

1184
01:14:39.716 --> 01:14:41.385
Um... Uh, just a minute!

1185
01:14:41.518 --> 01:14:43.487
Um, <i>ocupado.</i>

1186
01:14:43.620 --> 01:14:45.655
Whoa! Oh...

1187
01:14:46.690 --> 01:14:49.693
- Who are you?
- Gah! Oh!

1188
01:14:51.461 --> 01:14:53.663
Stay away.
I know Krav Maga.

1189
01:14:53.797 --> 01:14:55.999
Where you learn?
Shopping mall?

1190
01:14:57.167 --> 01:14:59.903
One! Two! Three!

1191
01:15:00.037 --> 01:15:01.638
Krav Maga! Yeah.

1192
01:15:06.977 --> 01:15:08.311
Don't shoot.

1193
01:15:08.445 --> 01:15:10.480
Jonny Australia,
the pleasure is all yours.

1194
01:15:14.351 --> 01:15:15.318
Come on.

1195
01:15:17.454 --> 01:15:19.189
Jane, where's
that sleepy-neck button?

1196
01:15:19.322 --> 01:15:21.091
<i>I'm a little busy.
Figure it out!</i>

1197
01:15:26.129 --> 01:15:27.564
Ooh!

1198
01:15:27.697 --> 01:15:29.266
Elena? Help me!

1199
01:15:33.236 --> 01:15:34.571
Ah!

1200
01:15:45.215 --> 01:15:46.416
Thanks, Elena.

1201
01:15:46.551 --> 01:15:48.251
I have dreamed of this moment

1202
01:15:48.385 --> 01:15:50.887
since the day I met you.
Except your hair was longer.

1203
01:15:51.021 --> 01:15:52.722
But I like this too.
This is great.

1204
01:15:58.662 --> 01:16:01.598
- Hey. Don't even think about it.
- You want to run away with me?

1205
01:16:01.731 --> 01:16:03.867
Oh, you're so desperate.

1206
01:16:04.000 --> 01:16:06.136
Hey, stop right... Elena!

1207
01:16:06.269 --> 01:16:07.572
I want to live
to see you again!

1208
01:16:07.704 --> 01:16:09.039
<i>Close the gate!</i>

1209
01:16:15.912 --> 01:16:16.813
Too late!

1210
01:16:25.590 --> 01:16:27.257
<i>Jane, where are you?!</i>

1211
01:16:27.390 --> 01:16:29.226
<i>The assassin's getting away!</i>

1212
01:16:44.641 --> 01:16:45.976
<i>Sabina!</i>

1213
01:16:48.979 --> 01:16:50.180
Uh...

1214
01:16:50.313 --> 01:16:51.381
Who are you?

1215
01:16:54.417 --> 01:16:56.153
Elena, stop this thing!

1216
01:16:56.286 --> 01:16:57.354
No!

1217
01:17:00.090 --> 01:17:01.191
Give me the case!

1218
01:17:07.297 --> 01:17:08.198
Oh!

1219
01:17:09.666 --> 01:17:11.034
<i>Elena?</i>

1220
01:17:12.836 --> 01:17:14.505
- Hold on!
- <i>Elena!</i>

1221
01:17:16.973 --> 01:17:17.974
Elena!

1222
01:17:21.945 --> 01:17:23.413
Oh, God. Oh, no!

1223
01:17:26.483 --> 01:17:29.554
Come on. Elena?
I need you, man! I need you!

1224
01:17:32.455 --> 01:17:34.625
Sabina, stay to the side!

1225
01:17:34.758 --> 01:17:35.959
Awesome!

1226
01:17:40.030 --> 01:17:41.965
Get me out of here!

1227
01:17:43.099 --> 01:17:44.234
Stop it!

1228
01:17:49.773 --> 01:17:51.141
Elena!

1229
01:17:53.343 --> 01:17:56.213
<i>It's about to get
very crush-y in here!</i>

1230
01:17:58.683 --> 01:18:00.317
Jane, we need you!

1231
01:18:00.450 --> 01:18:01.552
I've nearly got it!

1232
01:18:01.686 --> 01:18:03.688
<i>Jane, hurry!</i>

1233
01:18:03.820 --> 01:18:04.888
<i>Jane!</i>

1234
01:18:13.029 --> 01:18:14.364
I'm on my way.

1235
01:18:17.000 --> 01:18:18.001
Sabina,

1236
01:18:18.134 --> 01:18:19.269
<i>reach up.</i>

1237
01:18:26.544 --> 01:18:28.845
Jane! Jane!

1238
01:18:28.979 --> 01:18:30.914
This one! This one! There!

1239
01:18:37.521 --> 01:18:39.222
Oh, thank God.

1240
01:18:46.796 --> 01:18:47.797
Oh, God.

1241
01:18:47.931 --> 01:18:49.432
You all right, Sabina?!

1242
01:18:49.567 --> 01:18:51.301
Yeah. Better late than never.

1243
01:18:59.276 --> 01:19:01.111
Ha!

1244
01:19:01.244 --> 01:19:02.912
Oh, it's the wrong side.

1245
01:19:08.753 --> 01:19:10.954
Hey,
did the rookie just tranq herself?

1246
01:19:11.087 --> 01:19:12.355
Yup.

1247
01:19:14.057 --> 01:19:15.693
Where's your boyfriend?

1248
01:19:15.825 --> 01:19:19.095
- Hodak. The assassin?
- Gone.

1249
01:19:19.229 --> 01:19:20.964
Took Calisto with him.

1250
01:19:21.097 --> 01:19:23.534
- Where's Jonny?
- He scurried off.

1251
01:19:23.668 --> 01:19:25.770
He's a little bitch.

1252
01:19:25.902 --> 01:19:27.370
Where's Boz?

1253
01:19:32.142 --> 01:19:33.611
We probably
shouldn't be caught

1254
01:19:33.744 --> 01:19:35.145
standing over
a dead body.

1255
01:19:35.278 --> 01:19:37.748
Not dressed like this, no.

1256
01:20:02.305 --> 01:20:03.641
Is she dead?

1257
01:20:05.776 --> 01:20:07.511
You want to touch her?

1258
01:20:08.845 --> 01:20:10.480
Come on.

1259
01:20:10.614 --> 01:20:11.549
Touch her.

1260
01:20:14.785 --> 01:20:16.453
She feels alive!

1261
01:20:17.420 --> 01:20:18.955
You woke her up.

1262
01:20:20.857 --> 01:20:22.827
Hey, you.

1263
01:20:22.959 --> 01:20:24.461
Are we on a boat?

1264
01:20:25.830 --> 01:20:26.797
Yeah.

1265
01:20:49.553 --> 01:20:51.020
- Bosley!
- Boz?

1266
01:20:51.154 --> 01:20:52.889
Mrs. Bosley?

1267
01:20:58.696 --> 01:20:59.730
Boz.

1268
01:21:00.831 --> 01:21:02.365
Do Bosleys usually leave?

1269
01:21:03.834 --> 01:21:05.368
No, this is all wrong.

1270
01:21:06.771 --> 01:21:09.607
- So she's gone?
- Well, we were made,

1271
01:21:09.740 --> 01:21:11.307
so maybe she wanted
to do a sweep.

1272
01:21:13.109 --> 01:21:14.244
Maybe.

1273
01:21:16.346 --> 01:21:17.648
Or she's...

1274
01:21:19.583 --> 01:21:22.753
What? No.
Boz was the first Angel

1275
01:21:22.887 --> 01:21:24.954
to be promoted to Bosley.
She's one of us.

1276
01:21:25.088 --> 01:21:27.323
She would not be
the first Angel to turn.

1277
01:21:27.457 --> 01:21:29.225
It's happened.
You know the history.

1278
01:21:29.359 --> 01:21:31.629
It was her idea to steal Calisto
from the lab.

1279
01:21:31.762 --> 01:21:34.063
Exactly.
But Fleming beat her to it.

1280
01:21:34.197 --> 01:21:37.100
It's been our mission the entire
time to get this thing back,

1281
01:21:37.233 --> 01:21:39.469
and it just keeps
slipping us, like...

1282
01:21:39.603 --> 01:21:43.072
We're better than that.
It's... It's her.

1283
01:21:43.206 --> 01:21:45.375
Fleming's dead.
Calisto's gone.

1284
01:21:46.443 --> 01:21:47.977
And so is she.

1285
01:21:49.412 --> 01:21:51.749
Jonny said
he represented somebody...

1286
01:21:51.882 --> 01:21:53.249
What if it's Boz?

1287
01:21:58.221 --> 01:21:59.456
That's my room.

1288
01:22:05.629 --> 01:22:07.063
Hello?

1289
01:22:07.197 --> 01:22:09.834
Charlie sends love.
You're in grave danger.

1290
01:22:09.966 --> 01:22:12.135
- <i>Get out of there now!</i>
- Guys?

1291
01:22:31.622 --> 01:22:33.189
Jane?

1292
01:22:46.871 --> 01:22:49.005
Elena, stay down! Stay down!

1293
01:22:49.138 --> 01:22:50.574
Elena, stay down! Stay down!

1294
01:22:59.950 --> 01:23:01.150
I'm Bosley.

1295
01:23:01.284 --> 01:23:03.521
Let's get you out of here.

1296
01:23:03.654 --> 01:23:05.188
Quickly.

1297
01:23:43.192 --> 01:23:44.260
Sabina?

1298
01:23:47.397 --> 01:23:49.365
Sabina.

1299
01:23:49.499 --> 01:23:50.901
Sabina.

1300
01:24:01.011 --> 01:24:02.746
Hey. Sabina.

1301
01:24:21.065 --> 01:24:22.700
She means
a lot to you.

1302
01:24:23.934 --> 01:24:25.970
We're new friends.

1303
01:24:26.102 --> 01:24:27.370
I think.

1304
01:24:29.607 --> 01:24:32.442
It's been a really
tough week.

1305
01:24:38.214 --> 01:24:40.149
I can't lose her too.

1306
01:24:53.597 --> 01:24:55.099
What are you doing?

1307
01:24:55.231 --> 01:24:57.200
Oh! Oh, God.

1308
01:24:57.333 --> 01:24:59.703
- Ow!
- Oh, God, I'm sorry.

1309
01:24:59.837 --> 01:25:00.771
I'm so sorry.

1310
01:25:02.973 --> 01:25:04.775
Why are you crying?

1311
01:25:04.908 --> 01:25:07.511
Oh, I'm not crying. Heh.

1312
01:25:08.912 --> 01:25:10.446
Well, you are. That's...

1313
01:25:10.581 --> 01:25:11.782
That's what's...

1314
01:25:13.984 --> 01:25:16.053
Okay, fine, yeah,
I'm crying.

1315
01:25:17.755 --> 01:25:20.691
But I didn't think
that you...

1316
01:25:20.824 --> 01:25:22.026
cared about me.

1317
01:25:22.158 --> 01:25:23.961
Why?

1318
01:25:24.094 --> 01:25:25.495
Because...

1319
01:25:25.629 --> 01:25:27.798
Because you don't think
I have any feelings.

1320
01:25:27.931 --> 01:25:29.633
No, I...

1321
01:25:31.367 --> 01:25:34.138
I can be really annoying.

1322
01:25:34.270 --> 01:25:35.973
Most of the time.

1323
01:25:36.106 --> 01:25:38.207
You can be so annoying.

1324
01:25:38.341 --> 01:25:40.010
I don't try to be.
It just sort of...

1325
01:25:40.144 --> 01:25:42.146
I don't have the filter thing
people have.

1326
01:25:45.716 --> 01:25:47.183
- Hey.
- I don't know

1327
01:25:47.316 --> 01:25:50.721
what this is made of,
but it saved your life.

1328
01:25:50.854 --> 01:25:52.990
Thanks.

1329
01:25:53.123 --> 01:25:54.625
Where's Elena?

1330
01:25:54.758 --> 01:25:56.160
I don't know.

1331
01:25:56.292 --> 01:25:59.163
We have to find her,
so I called in for some help.

1332
01:25:59.295 --> 01:26:02.365
- Because I got blown up?
- Yeah.

1333
01:26:04.267 --> 01:26:06.503
But also because...

1334
01:26:06.637 --> 01:26:09.907
you convinced me I don't
have to do everything by myself.

1335
01:26:10.040 --> 01:26:11.240
Well done.

1336
01:26:12.943 --> 01:26:16.180
Hello, Angels.
You owe me an explanation.

1337
01:26:16.312 --> 01:26:18.649
This is not Brazil.

1338
01:26:18.782 --> 01:26:21.051
- Hey.
- I brought supplies.

1339
01:26:21.185 --> 01:26:23.020
Homemade kombucha
with probiotics.

1340
01:26:23.153 --> 01:26:24.722
And the best part...

1341
01:26:24.855 --> 01:26:26.389
I brought a friend.

1342
01:26:26.523 --> 01:26:27.524
You.
You trai...

1343
01:26:27.658 --> 01:26:29.225
- Hey!
- Jane.

1344
01:26:29.358 --> 01:26:30.661
I'm not the mole.

1345
01:26:30.794 --> 01:26:31.762
Then why are you here?

1346
01:26:31.895 --> 01:26:33.831
The same reason you are.

1347
01:26:33.964 --> 01:26:35.899
I should be dead.

1348
01:26:40.336 --> 01:26:42.106
She called me
right after you did.

1349
01:26:42.238 --> 01:26:44.340
I have an herbal compress
for the bruises.

1350
01:26:44.474 --> 01:26:47.276
- Nobody wants that.
- Okay. Keep your bruises.

1351
01:26:47.410 --> 01:26:48.879
So then who?

1352
01:26:50.480 --> 01:26:52.716
- Make yourself at home.
- Thank you.

1353
01:26:55.119 --> 01:26:56.720
I had some clothes sent up.

1354
01:26:56.854 --> 01:26:58.387
Take your pick.

1355
01:27:01.892 --> 01:27:04.728
Um, why so formal?

1356
01:27:04.862 --> 01:27:07.798
I'm sorry, is this
another headquarters?

1357
01:27:07.931 --> 01:27:11.400
Have you heard from Jane
and Sabina? Will they come?

1358
01:27:11.535 --> 01:27:13.436
So inquisitive.

1359
01:27:13.570 --> 01:27:15.471
Curiosity of a cat.

1360
01:27:15.606 --> 01:27:17.174
Or a ferret.

1361
01:27:17.306 --> 01:27:19.076
It's the scientist in you,
isn't it?

1362
01:27:20.978 --> 01:27:23.279
Just trying
to understand my situation.

1363
01:27:23.412 --> 01:27:27.283
You wanted an audience with
Mr. Brok to discuss Calisto.

1364
01:27:27.416 --> 01:27:29.987
Well, soon you'll have one.

1365
01:27:30.120 --> 01:27:32.321
But Calisto's
been stolen now, so I...

1366
01:27:46.136 --> 01:27:47.638
Well done.

1367
01:27:49.673 --> 01:27:52.609
Satisfying when a plan
comes together.

1368
01:27:52.743 --> 01:27:55.444
We'll give you some privacy.

1369
01:27:56.613 --> 01:27:57.948
Oh, my...

1370
01:28:01.919 --> 01:28:04.154
- No way.
- Oh, yes.

1371
01:28:04.288 --> 01:28:05.789
I've been tracking him
for weeks.

1372
01:28:05.923 --> 01:28:07.291
<i>When he landed in Istanbul,</i>

1373
01:28:07.423 --> 01:28:08.992
<i>I knew I needed to get to him</i>

1374
01:28:09.126 --> 01:28:10.694
<i>before he got to you.</i>

1375
01:28:10.828 --> 01:28:13.329
<i>Boz, they are leaving.
Go, no-go?</i>

1376
01:28:15.966 --> 01:28:17.301
<i>Boz.</i>

1377
01:28:17.433 --> 01:28:18.669
Damn it!

1378
01:28:18.802 --> 01:28:21.038
I'm sorry I left
the quarry, but...

1379
01:28:21.171 --> 01:28:23.040
more sorry I was too late.

1380
01:28:23.173 --> 01:28:26.176
I just can't believe that.
A Bosley?

1381
01:28:26.310 --> 01:28:28.979
Mm, you had no trouble
believing it was me.

1382
01:28:29.112 --> 01:28:31.148
- You heard that?
- Mm.

1383
01:28:31.281 --> 01:28:33.283
Australian Jonny.

1384
01:28:33.416 --> 01:28:36.320
- The one that got away.
- Yeah, again.

1385
01:28:36.452 --> 01:28:37.988
The last time we saw him,

1386
01:28:38.121 --> 01:28:40.557
- we were in Rio, and then...
- You pushed me off a roof.

1387
01:28:40.691 --> 01:28:42.726
- You have got to get over that.
- Oh, my God.

1388
01:28:42.860 --> 01:28:45.428
I am. Just processing.

1389
01:28:45.562 --> 01:28:47.698
So then the last person
to see him was...

1390
01:28:47.831 --> 01:28:49.398
- Was Bosley.
- Exactly.

1391
01:28:49.533 --> 01:28:51.068
When Jonny
didn't make it to jail,

1392
01:28:51.201 --> 01:28:53.036
Charlie suspected
Bosley had gone rogue.

1393
01:28:53.170 --> 01:28:55.305
It turns out
he's building his own network,

1394
01:28:55.438 --> 01:28:57.473
selling his services
to the highest bidders.

1395
01:28:57.608 --> 01:28:59.276
He's using us
to date criminals now?

1396
01:28:59.408 --> 01:29:04.281
Yeah. Jonny, Mr. Hodak, that
assassin, they work for Bosley.

1397
01:29:04.413 --> 01:29:06.783
He always seemed like
kind of a weirdo.

1398
01:29:06.917 --> 01:29:08.752
Freaky. English.

1399
01:29:10.220 --> 01:29:11.922
- So Bosley has Elena.
- Mm-hm.

1400
01:29:12.055 --> 01:29:14.057
- Do we know where?
- Of course we know.

1401
01:29:14.191 --> 01:29:16.860
There's trackers
in most of the clothes.

1402
01:29:16.994 --> 01:29:19.563
You have a lot of leather
jackets at your apartment.

1403
01:29:19.696 --> 01:29:22.699
- See, I told you it was borrow and not take.
- Shh shh...

1404
01:29:22.833 --> 01:29:26.303
Brok is hosting a party
at his compound. Elena's there.

1405
01:29:29.239 --> 01:29:31.875
<i>Every year, he brings together
the wealthy and beautiful</i>

1406
01:29:32.009 --> 01:29:34.544
<i>for his annual Vision Party.</i>

1407
01:29:34.678 --> 01:29:37.714
<i>This year, he's planning to
present Calisto to investors.</i>

1408
01:29:37.848 --> 01:29:39.983
Why would Bosley want
to take Elena to Brok?

1409
01:29:40.117 --> 01:29:43.654
Bringing the Birdman
back to Alcatraz, I guess.

1410
01:29:44.788 --> 01:29:45.989
The who?

1411
01:29:47.423 --> 01:29:49.293
It's a movie.
Burt Lancaster.

1412
01:29:49.425 --> 01:29:51.328
<i>Birdman.</i> Michael Keaton.

1413
01:29:51.460 --> 01:29:54.430
- No, Michael Keaton is Batman.
- No, Ben Affleck is Batman.

1414
01:29:54.564 --> 01:29:56.400
I mean, is he?

1415
01:29:56.533 --> 01:29:59.269
Am I the only person here
who knows who Burt Lancaster is?

1416
01:29:59.403 --> 01:30:00.804
- I'm concussed.
- Doesn't matter.

1417
01:30:00.938 --> 01:30:03.140
- It's an old movie. It's from...
- How old are you?

1418
01:30:03.273 --> 01:30:05.642
How old am I? What?
That has nothing to do with it.

1419
01:30:05.776 --> 01:30:08.111
- I don't have your references.
- There are film buffs

1420
01:30:08.245 --> 01:30:10.446
- of all ages.
- Let's go get our girl.

1421
01:30:16.520 --> 01:30:17.988
What do you want with me?

1422
01:30:35.739 --> 01:30:38.008
Did you raid
your mom's closet for this?

1423
01:30:39.543 --> 01:30:41.678
What else of hers
do you play with?

1424
01:30:49.386 --> 01:30:53.991
I've spent an entire career
estimating the talents of women.

1425
01:30:54.124 --> 01:30:57.160
And you, my dear,

1426
01:30:57.294 --> 01:30:59.663
are marvelously clever.

1427
01:31:00.831 --> 01:31:02.132
You betrayed them.

1428
01:31:02.265 --> 01:31:04.034
You betrayed the Angels.

1429
01:31:04.167 --> 01:31:07.037
Well, I no longer work
for the Townsend Agency.

1430
01:31:07.170 --> 01:31:10.073
I was retired.

1431
01:31:10.207 --> 01:31:14.211
So you are going
to show me

1432
01:31:14.344 --> 01:31:17.848
how to hack this
and reprogram root access...

1433
01:31:18.949 --> 01:31:20.417
to me.

1434
01:31:20.550 --> 01:31:22.719
You thought Fleming
could do it.

1435
01:31:22.853 --> 01:31:24.755
He always had a habit
of claiming credit

1436
01:31:24.888 --> 01:31:26.423
he didn't deserve.

1437
01:31:26.556 --> 01:31:29.059
- How long will it take?
- Forever. I'm not touching it.

1438
01:31:31.361 --> 01:31:33.897
Ha, ha, you think
you have a choice.

1439
01:31:34.031 --> 01:31:35.565
It's adorable.

1440
01:31:35.699 --> 01:31:38.168
They'll send...
They'll send love.

1441
01:31:41.538 --> 01:31:43.907
They'll send love.

1442
01:31:45.342 --> 01:31:48.545
Ooh, feisty.
You've been studying.

1443
01:31:51.516 --> 01:31:54.017
I hope they come.

1444
01:32:09.666 --> 01:32:12.736
<i>The compound has
nearly 60 rooms on four levels.</i>

1445
01:32:12.869 --> 01:32:15.705
<i>There's 36 security guards
contracted for the party,</i>

1446
01:32:15.839 --> 01:32:17.340
<i>plus Brok's private crew.</i>

1447
01:32:30.387 --> 01:32:31.788
That's my song!

1448
01:33:04.387 --> 01:33:06.056
Oh, did you want one?

1449
01:33:07.824 --> 01:33:10.827
- I'm good.
- Okay, let's do this.

1450
01:33:10.961 --> 01:33:13.830
<i>Elena's being held on the top
floor, northwest corner.</i>

1451
01:33:13.964 --> 01:33:15.832
<i>She's our priority.</i>

1452
01:33:44.261 --> 01:33:47.565
- Oop! Hey.
- This is a private floor.

1453
01:33:47.697 --> 01:33:49.833
I'm just turned around.
This place is huge.

1454
01:33:49.966 --> 01:33:51.502
I was looking for
the bathroom.

1455
01:33:51.636 --> 01:33:53.638
It's just that
I really need to pee.

1456
01:33:53.770 --> 01:33:56.239
Am I in the wrong place?
I thought may...

1457
01:33:59.142 --> 01:34:00.343
Sweet dreams.

1458
01:34:02.445 --> 01:34:03.680
We're in.

1459
01:34:04.714 --> 01:34:06.149
Why are you doing this?

1460
01:34:06.283 --> 01:34:09.886
To neutralize an enemy
discreetly and anonymously.

1461
01:34:10.020 --> 01:34:12.322
That's a gold standard
in my business.

1462
01:34:12.455 --> 01:34:15.325
What you deem a flaw,
I deem a gift.

1463
01:34:15.458 --> 01:34:19.564
One that not only
provides power...

1464
01:34:19.729 --> 01:34:21.364
but confers it as well.

1465
01:34:24.134 --> 01:34:25.969
Whoa, what are you doing
in my office?

1466
01:34:26.102 --> 01:34:28.539
Mr. Brok? Oh, my God.
Thank God. Please help me.

1467
01:34:28.673 --> 01:34:30.307
- What is she doing here?
- These men...

1468
01:34:34.277 --> 01:34:37.480
John, I'm a little confused.
I thought you handled her.

1469
01:34:37.615 --> 01:34:39.482
Handled me?

1470
01:34:42.452 --> 01:34:43.554
It was you?

1471
01:34:43.688 --> 01:34:45.889
You wanted to sabotage me.

1472
01:34:46.022 --> 01:34:48.158
What were you expecting,
flowers?

1473
01:34:48.291 --> 01:34:49.926
A handwritten thank-you note?

1474
01:34:51.529 --> 01:34:53.930
Get rid of her already.

1475
01:34:54.064 --> 01:34:57.434
Actually, I believe
that she can still prove useful.

1476
01:34:57.568 --> 01:35:03.273
- Do you even know who he is?
- Yes. My global security chief.

1477
01:35:03.406 --> 01:35:06.343
John's just recovered Calisto
from Peter Fleming,

1478
01:35:06.476 --> 01:35:08.278
that shortsighted,
greedy traitor.

1479
01:35:08.411 --> 01:35:10.747
They killed him.
They killed Fleming.

1480
01:35:10.880 --> 01:35:12.550
Whoa, whoa,
la-la-la-la-la!

1481
01:35:12.683 --> 01:35:14.384
This is the problem
with you, right?

1482
01:35:14.518 --> 01:35:17.287
You keep telling me shit
I can't know.

1483
01:35:17.420 --> 01:35:20.390
Plausible deniability.
You ever heard of it?

1484
01:35:20.524 --> 01:35:21.791
You're a terrible employee.

1485
01:35:21.925 --> 01:35:23.793
Yeah, and who cares
if people die, right?

1486
01:35:23.927 --> 01:35:25.495
As long as the investors
are happy.

1487
01:35:25.630 --> 01:35:26.830
Grow up, little girl.

1488
01:35:26.963 --> 01:35:29.232
Calisto is about
to change the world.

1489
01:35:29.366 --> 01:35:33.003
If you want to bake a cake,
you got to break a few eggs.

1490
01:35:33.136 --> 01:35:35.839
It's omelet. If you're gonna
compare dead people to eggs,

1491
01:35:35.972 --> 01:35:38.174
could you at least use
the correct phrase?

1492
01:35:38.308 --> 01:35:41.646
I shouldn't be here, ha, ha.
You're a security threat.

1493
01:35:41.778 --> 01:35:44.180
You take care of her
and finish what you started.

1494
01:35:44.314 --> 01:35:45.815
That's exactly the plan.

1495
01:35:48.885 --> 01:35:50.688
Oh, excuse me.
I have a party to host.

1496
01:35:52.155 --> 01:35:56.426
- Yo, Tats, move.
- Take a seat, Mr. Brok.

1497
01:35:58.094 --> 01:35:59.664
Uh, no.

1498
01:35:59.829 --> 01:36:02.499
Sorry, what
the hell's happening here?

1499
01:36:02.633 --> 01:36:03.967
Oh, my God.

1500
01:36:05.101 --> 01:36:06.671
Let me out now.

1501
01:36:10.273 --> 01:36:12.008
Sorry, you work for me.

1502
01:36:12.142 --> 01:36:15.245
All right,
all of you work for me!

1503
01:36:17.247 --> 01:36:18.481
You dumbass. Ha, ha.

1504
01:36:18.616 --> 01:36:20.183
Why are you laughing?

1505
01:36:20.317 --> 01:36:21.985
You idiot.

1506
01:36:22.118 --> 01:36:24.454
They're stealing
Calisto from you.

1507
01:36:24.588 --> 01:36:28.693
They're gonna use it as
a weapon. To assassinate people.

1508
01:36:47.110 --> 01:36:48.211
Beep, bop, bloop.

1509
01:36:48.345 --> 01:36:50.180
Bloop, beep, bloop,
boop, boop!

1510
01:36:53.584 --> 01:36:55.820
- That ought to do it.
- I think so.

1511
01:36:57.454 --> 01:37:00.223
If you would grant root access,
please, Mr. Brok.

1512
01:37:00.357 --> 01:37:02.660
Heh, you're crazy.
Heh, heh.

1513
01:37:02.793 --> 01:37:04.894
I'm not giving you
my access.

1514
01:37:05.028 --> 01:37:06.697
You could alter
the blockchain.

1515
01:37:06.831 --> 01:37:09.667
You could ruin it. You could
literally ruin everything.

1516
01:37:09.800 --> 01:37:12.168
Ow! Ow!

1517
01:37:12.302 --> 01:37:15.205
Our intention is
for Calisto to be released

1518
01:37:15.338 --> 01:37:17.407
into the market as planned.

1519
01:37:17.541 --> 01:37:20.043
In fact, the more units
there are out there

1520
01:37:20.176 --> 01:37:22.178
for me to hack into,
the better.

1521
01:37:22.312 --> 01:37:23.913
Don't do it.
They've killed everyone

1522
01:37:24.047 --> 01:37:26.416
who knows about this
except you and me.

1523
01:37:26.550 --> 01:37:29.854
Mr. Brok is complicit
in the deaths of two people.

1524
01:37:29.986 --> 01:37:33.123
- Oh...
- Now, I am very happy

1525
01:37:33.256 --> 01:37:36.359
to inform my former colleagues
in law enforcement.

1526
01:37:42.232 --> 01:37:43.768
<i>Hello, Alexander.</i>

1527
01:37:43.900 --> 01:37:45.569
<i>Root access granted.</i>

1528
01:37:45.703 --> 01:37:47.937
<i>♪ All I do is win, win, win ♪</i>

1529
01:37:48.071 --> 01:37:49.740
<i>♪ No matter what
Got money on my mind ♪</i>

1530
01:37:49.874 --> 01:37:51.374
<i>♪ I can never get it off ♪</i>

1531
01:37:51.509 --> 01:37:53.076
Do you want to answer that?

1532
01:37:54.545 --> 01:37:56.079
No.

1533
01:37:57.882 --> 01:37:59.916
<i>♪ All I do is win, win, win
No matter what ♪</i>

1534
01:38:00.049 --> 01:38:01.451
Yes.

1535
01:38:01.585 --> 01:38:04.555
<i>♪ ...on my mind
I can never get it off ♪</i>

1536
01:38:04.688 --> 01:38:06.891
Oh, great.
It's an attempted access alert

1537
01:38:07.023 --> 01:38:09.225
on my personal safe.

1538
01:38:10.927 --> 01:38:12.996
You're up, my dear.

1539
01:38:13.129 --> 01:38:14.330
Go to hell.

1540
01:38:16.266 --> 01:38:20.738
Well, let me see
if I can change your mind.

1541
01:38:20.871 --> 01:38:25.408
Perhaps if I gave you
another delightful surprise.

1542
01:38:25.543 --> 01:38:27.210
♪ Ah ♪

1543
01:38:29.513 --> 01:38:31.247
Langston. Oh, my God.

1544
01:38:32.949 --> 01:38:35.285
He's been in there
all the time.

1545
01:38:35.418 --> 01:38:38.756
You hid a person
in my Louis XIV?

1546
01:38:38.889 --> 01:38:40.990
What is wrong with you?

1547
01:38:41.124 --> 01:38:43.426
No sense of humor,
that's your problem.

1548
01:39:29.038 --> 01:39:30.508
I was hoping
it would be you.

1549
01:39:33.844 --> 01:39:35.880
- Bitch.
- Fair warning.

1550
01:39:36.012 --> 01:39:38.214
Since we last met,
I made a friend.

1551
01:39:42.820 --> 01:39:44.487
Jane, what's the update?

1552
01:39:44.622 --> 01:39:46.857
<i>Yeah!
We're almost done with him.</i>

1553
01:39:46.991 --> 01:39:48.491
You sit tight.

1554
01:39:56.232 --> 01:39:58.401
Switching root access.

1555
01:40:00.538 --> 01:40:02.740
Name and thumbprint.

1556
01:40:02.873 --> 01:40:04.207
John Bosley.

1557
01:40:04.340 --> 01:40:07.678
<i>Hello, John.
Root access granted.</i>

1558
01:40:07.811 --> 01:40:10.280
- Done.
- Good girl.

1559
01:40:10.413 --> 01:40:14.384
I'll have to check, of course,
that it's actually working.

1560
01:40:14.518 --> 01:40:17.220
Calisto, short-range
power burst.

1561
01:40:17.353 --> 01:40:19.757
- No override.
- Ah, whoa, whoa!

1562
01:40:19.890 --> 01:40:22.058
What are you doing?
It will kill us.

1563
01:40:22.191 --> 01:40:24.028
Don't be daft.
It will kill her.

1564
01:40:24.160 --> 01:40:27.430
And what's-his-name. Not us.

1565
01:40:27.565 --> 01:40:31.035
We're gonna be downstairs
enjoying your party. Come on.

1566
01:40:31.167 --> 01:40:34.672
You want me to go down there
and pretend everything's fine?

1567
01:40:34.805 --> 01:40:36.172
Everything is fine.

1568
01:40:36.306 --> 01:40:39.743
You're gonna disrupt
the power industry!

1569
01:40:39.877 --> 01:40:41.545
Go, you.

1570
01:40:41.679 --> 01:40:45.015
You know, retirement
is better than I expected.

1571
01:40:53.824 --> 01:40:56.225
I'm so sorry, Langston.
Oh, God!

1572
01:40:56.359 --> 01:40:57.895
Ah!

1573
01:40:58.028 --> 01:40:59.462
That guy is a total dick.

1574
01:41:08.572 --> 01:41:11.742
- Did you get it?
- Yeah, girl, I got you.

1575
01:41:11.875 --> 01:41:13.209
Of course I got it.

1576
01:41:16.714 --> 01:41:18.448
Have fun, guys.

1577
01:41:18.582 --> 01:41:19.984
See ya!

1578
01:41:25.689 --> 01:41:27.290
- Excuse me. Sorry!
- Hey.

1579
01:41:27.423 --> 01:41:29.927
Whoop! Yow!

1580
01:41:30.060 --> 01:41:33.162
This is your party, Alex.
Enjoy it.

1581
01:41:35.633 --> 01:41:38.201
The world is on fire, Alex.

1582
01:41:38.334 --> 01:41:41.437
But I'm sure your generation
is gonna figure it out.

1583
01:41:45.609 --> 01:41:49.613
- Hey, help us!
- There must be a key somewhere.

1584
01:41:51.849 --> 01:41:53.984
You see, it was
my mentor, Edgar,

1585
01:41:54.118 --> 01:41:56.152
who taught me
how to win a fight.

1586
01:41:56.285 --> 01:41:59.489
You thought you beat me
twice before? No.

1587
01:41:59.623 --> 01:42:00.891
I was learning.

1588
01:42:25.314 --> 01:42:27.350
You've got seven moves,
Mr. Hodak.

1589
01:42:34.257 --> 01:42:35.726
I know them all.

1590
01:42:55.112 --> 01:42:56.880
Seven moves...

1591
01:42:57.014 --> 01:42:58.082
and a fragile ego.

1592
01:43:07.290 --> 01:43:10.060
Why is this happening?!

1593
01:43:22.806 --> 01:43:24.908
- Got her.
- <i>Good job.</i>

1594
01:43:26.342 --> 01:43:28.277
- Yes! Oh, ho, ho!
- Sabina! Oh, my God.

1595
01:43:28.411 --> 01:43:30.748
You came for me.
Look at you.

1596
01:43:30.881 --> 01:43:33.449
- Why is that thing doing that?
- Oh, that? That's nothing.

1597
01:43:33.584 --> 01:43:35.919
I just programmed it
to light up and make noises.

1598
01:43:38.222 --> 01:43:39.388
You two, with me.

1599
01:43:41.625 --> 01:43:43.894
Directly to the exit, please.
Get this man help.

1600
01:43:44.027 --> 01:43:47.631
Calm down. Get out.
Everybody go.

1601
01:43:47.765 --> 01:43:49.233
Just get out.

1602
01:43:54.238 --> 01:43:56.439
Do you really think
you'd kill me, old badger?

1603
01:43:56.573 --> 01:43:58.942
You know, Rebecca,
I really did.

1604
01:44:01.145 --> 01:44:03.147
My name is Bosley,

1605
01:44:03.279 --> 01:44:04.681
and I'm gonna kick your ass.

1606
01:44:08.986 --> 01:44:11.688
You expect me to go quietly
after 40 years?

1607
01:44:14.625 --> 01:44:16.994
This is what I do.

1608
01:44:31.108 --> 01:44:32.609
You're outmanned, Angel.

1609
01:44:33.644 --> 01:44:35.478
You always have been.

1610
01:44:37.781 --> 01:44:39.348
Kill her.

1611
01:44:42.286 --> 01:44:43.854
Send the love.

1612
01:45:16.186 --> 01:45:17.154
Ingrid?

1613
01:45:33.503 --> 01:45:34.872
You've been busy.

1614
01:45:35.005 --> 01:45:36.673
How did you...?

1615
01:45:37.741 --> 01:45:39.676
It's just business, John.

1616
01:45:43.013 --> 01:45:44.181
He's with me now.

1617
01:45:44.314 --> 01:45:46.116
I see.

1618
01:45:46.250 --> 01:45:49.953
You know, I built this agency
from the ground up.

1619
01:45:50.087 --> 01:45:53.290
It was supposed to be mine
after Charlie died.

1620
01:45:53.422 --> 01:45:55.592
I was pushed out.

1621
01:45:55.726 --> 01:46:00.297
What did you expect me to do?
Take up gardening?

1622
01:46:00.463 --> 01:46:03.867
You thought you made us.
We made you.

1623
01:46:04.001 --> 01:46:07.371
- Yeah, we trusted you, you dick.
- Good nigh...

1624
01:46:07.504 --> 01:46:09.072
I was in the middle
of my speech.

1625
01:46:09.206 --> 01:46:10.406
Sorry.

1626
01:46:11.541 --> 01:46:12.709
All right, well...

1627
01:46:12.843 --> 01:46:16.079
Sweep it clean, Angels.
Good job.

1628
01:46:22.853 --> 01:46:26.790
So you want to go to California
and train to be an Angel?

1629
01:46:26.924 --> 01:46:28.625
What? I...

1630
01:46:28.759 --> 01:46:30.661
Really? You...

1631
01:46:34.965 --> 01:46:37.100
- Oh, my God.
- We are recruiting you.

1632
01:46:37.234 --> 01:46:38.802
To be an Angel like...

1633
01:46:38.936 --> 01:46:40.436
- you and Jane?
- Let's go.

1634
01:46:40.570 --> 01:46:42.471
What do you
think we've been doing?

1635
01:46:42.606 --> 01:46:43.707
I don't know.

1636
01:46:43.840 --> 01:46:44.875
I thought you were smart.

1637
01:46:45.008 --> 01:46:46.910
Isn't that your thing?

1638
01:46:47.044 --> 01:46:48.477
<i>It's done, Charlie.</i>

1639
01:46:48.612 --> 01:46:51.081
<i>And I decided what to do
with Elena Houghlin.</i>

1640
01:46:51.214 --> 01:46:53.317
- <i>What's that?</i>
- <i>She's our new recruit.</i>

1641
01:46:53.449 --> 01:46:54.885
Good. Thank you, Boz.

1642
01:46:55.018 --> 01:46:56.386
<i>Good. Thank you, Boz.</i>

1643
01:46:56.520 --> 01:46:57.921
I appreciate the call.

1644
01:46:58.055 --> 01:46:59.389
<i>I appreciate the call.</i>

1645
01:47:01.224 --> 01:47:04.294
- What do you do in California?
- Ever jumped out of a plane?

1646
01:47:04.428 --> 01:47:06.797
- I don't really do heights.
- Oh, um...

1647
01:47:06.930 --> 01:47:08.799
- Have you swam with sharks?
- Hey! It's you.

1648
01:47:08.932 --> 01:47:10.466
How long can you
hold your breath?

1649
01:47:10.600 --> 01:47:12.468
Sharks? Not long.

1650
01:47:12.602 --> 01:47:13.937
- Oh, hey.
- Hi.

1651
01:47:14.071 --> 01:47:15.906
What happened to you?

1652
01:47:16.039 --> 01:47:18.275
Wait, you guys
know each other?

1653
01:47:18.408 --> 01:47:20.344
- Yeah, I was eating a sandwich.
- Yeah.

1654
01:47:20.476 --> 01:47:22.779
- I came in, and you gave me the...
- The phosphorus.

1655
01:47:22.913 --> 01:47:24.514
That's my favorite
chemical.

1656
01:47:24.648 --> 01:47:27.017
- Because you were...
- Exactly, mixed with...

1657
01:47:27.150 --> 01:47:30.153
Um, did you...?

1658
01:47:30.287 --> 01:47:32.589
Did you do that?

1659
01:47:32.723 --> 01:47:34.858
Oh, uh, yeah.

1660
01:47:34.992 --> 01:47:38.028
I think he, uh,
finally got the point.

1661
01:47:38.161 --> 01:47:41.031
Is that a pun?
Because you impaled him?

1662
01:47:41.164 --> 01:47:45.702
Are you doing, like, a joke
thing for the handsome nerd?

1663
01:47:45.836 --> 01:47:48.038
- Of course not.
- I mean, it's working,

1664
01:47:48.171 --> 01:47:50.407
if that is
what you're doing.

1665
01:47:50.540 --> 01:47:52.576
So if I'm trying
to get in touch with you,

1666
01:47:52.709 --> 01:47:56.046
- how would I do that?
- Oh, don't worry. I'll find you.

1667
01:48:03.387 --> 01:48:04.988
You did that?

1668
01:48:06.456 --> 01:48:08.325
Yeah.

1669
01:48:08.458 --> 01:48:09.926
Elena Houghlin.

1670
01:48:10.060 --> 01:48:11.595
Kelly Garrett.

1671
01:48:11.728 --> 01:48:13.330
Welcome to the Townsend Agency.

1672
01:48:26.743 --> 01:48:28.945
You lifted coming
into the last corner.

1673
01:48:29.079 --> 01:48:31.214
You got to trust it.
Go again.

1674
01:48:44.795 --> 01:48:46.930
Hands up. No fear.

1675
01:48:47.064 --> 01:48:48.398
Fight through the pain.

1676
01:48:48.533 --> 01:48:49.733
Focus.

1677
01:48:49.866 --> 01:48:51.768
Try to last
90 seconds this time.

1678
01:49:01.578 --> 01:49:04.714
You must clip the wires

1679
01:49:04.848 --> 01:49:08.185
in the correct order,
or you will...

1680
01:49:08.318 --> 01:49:09.753
- Done!
- ...blow up.

1681
01:49:14.724 --> 01:49:16.561
Good job not dying,
Houghlin.

1682
01:49:16.693 --> 01:49:18.695
The rest of you,
clean up and start again.

1683
01:49:24.034 --> 01:49:27.404
Houghlin, get up! Let's go!
Ten seconds to jump!

1684
01:49:27.538 --> 01:49:29.372
- Everybody up!
- Okay.

1685
01:49:29.507 --> 01:49:32.242
I'm not freaking terrified
at all! Let's go!

1686
01:49:32.375 --> 01:49:34.211
Heaven above,
watch over us today.

1687
01:49:34.344 --> 01:49:35.979
Don't make me a literal angel.

1688
01:49:36.113 --> 01:49:38.648
I've been training for
this moment my whole life!

1689
01:49:38.782 --> 01:49:42.452
All right, recruits!
One final challenge!

1690
01:49:42.587 --> 01:49:46.289
When Ruth Bader Ginsburg
made this jump in '99...

1691
01:49:46.423 --> 01:49:48.191
RBG is an Angel?

1692
01:49:48.325 --> 01:49:49.993
Forget I said that!

1693
01:49:50.127 --> 01:49:51.628
Let's make it happen!

1694
01:49:51.761 --> 01:49:53.997
Be the love!

1695
01:49:54.131 --> 01:49:56.800
Go, Chloe, go! Let's go!

1696
01:49:59.604 --> 01:50:01.872
Get out of there!
Let's go!

1697
01:50:05.175 --> 01:50:07.512
Where do you think
you're going?

1698
01:50:07.644 --> 01:50:09.547
You need to land
this bird, Houghlin.

1699
01:50:09.679 --> 01:50:11.448
I hope I see you
on the ground.

1700
01:50:11.582 --> 01:50:14.484
I really, really do.

1701
01:50:14.619 --> 01:50:16.119
Later.

1702
01:50:24.161 --> 01:50:25.228
Shit!

1703
01:50:25.362 --> 01:50:27.164
Shit. Okay, okay.

1704
01:50:27.297 --> 01:50:28.566
Oh, my God.

1705
01:50:28.698 --> 01:50:30.066
Okay.

1706
01:50:31.368 --> 01:50:33.803
- Oh, I've missed her!
- Yes, yes!

1707
01:50:33.937 --> 01:50:35.739
That's it, baby!
Bring her down!

1708
01:50:36.840 --> 01:50:39.009
- Yes, yes, yes!
- Yeah!

1709
01:50:40.343 --> 01:50:42.412
- Woo-hoo!
- Yes!

1710
01:50:42.547 --> 01:50:44.247
Whoo!

1711
01:50:46.716 --> 01:50:48.885
- There she is!
- Yes!

1712
01:50:49.019 --> 01:50:50.621
Good job. You did it!

1713
01:50:52.088 --> 01:50:53.290
Thank you for coming.

1714
01:50:53.423 --> 01:50:54.659
- Of course you did.
- I landed.

1715
01:50:54.791 --> 01:50:55.959
Dude, we weren't worried.

1716
01:50:56.092 --> 01:50:57.160
- A little worried.
- I know.

1717
01:50:57.294 --> 01:50:58.862
Let me smell your breath.

1718
01:50:58.995 --> 01:51:00.531
- She didn't even puke!
- Oh!

1719
01:51:00.665 --> 01:51:02.132
Oh, my gosh.

1720
01:51:02.265 --> 01:51:03.466
Yeah!

1721
01:51:58.955 --> 01:52:02.593
Okay! Sign the chair, make it
official. Don't think about it.

1722
01:52:02.727 --> 01:52:04.995
Here we go, here we go.
Shots, shots, shots!

1723
01:52:05.128 --> 01:52:06.496
- Please, please, please.
- Yeah!

1724
01:52:06.631 --> 01:52:08.198
You made it through training.

1725
01:52:08.331 --> 01:52:10.233
Okay, I'm so nervous,
you guys.

1726
01:52:10.367 --> 01:52:11.468
- Oh, my God!
- Here.

1727
01:52:11.602 --> 01:52:13.970
- Oh, shots. I need it.
- That'll help.

1728
01:52:15.305 --> 01:52:17.140
Okay.

1729
01:52:17.274 --> 01:52:18.341
Voilà.

1730
01:52:18.475 --> 01:52:20.176
You ready?
Ass in the chair, lady.

1731
01:52:20.310 --> 01:52:22.479
- Let's go.
- Okay, okay.

1732
01:52:22.613 --> 01:52:24.481
Oh, God. Guys,
I think I want mine there.

1733
01:52:24.615 --> 01:52:27.183
Is that a good place? I don't
think that hurts as much.

1734
01:52:27.317 --> 01:52:29.754
- That's very sweet.
- Okay, on a scale of one to 10,

1735
01:52:29.886 --> 01:52:31.354
how much does it hurt?
Be honest.

1736
01:52:31.488 --> 01:52:33.123
- Just tell me.
- I no longer feel pain.

1737
01:52:33.256 --> 01:52:35.125
Less than a bullet,
more than a piercing.

1738
01:52:35.258 --> 01:52:37.460
Great. I have no reference
for that. Thank you.

1739
01:52:37.595 --> 01:52:40.096
- <i>Good morning, Angels.</i>
- Good morning, Charlie.

1740
01:52:40.230 --> 01:52:41.965
<i>Elena, congratulations.</i>

1741
01:52:42.098 --> 01:52:43.366
Thank you, Charlie.

1742
01:52:43.501 --> 01:52:45.835
All right.
I'm ready if you are.

1743
01:52:47.971 --> 01:52:50.508
Hell, yeah.
Give me my wings.
